ified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqUABwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjqsQAEXk6a6/sC7MoELb1tz3VMh+\nPQjkk0vwm4HbAyGupqvECOBS13fO7nH8B6p8PO+5r6yTuY7l8ZKxLTCGIaM2hnCB\nuW2FtiZx+AEIflakQcbTcZSw58lh2s2H+76AMiHOOlFhVXZLty3XYZQXF+E4OY1a\ne18H/Xcb3p1tQ8bDVuRfFeFx0usI9sxtAJB0r+g+cfNo/mhqodw+l93LjTrWZuZi\nAKL7iTY3AiZYcMa4d1LNrbsnywDw7gjPKoMp3oX7jthDiB8vZrXNF6kKb0DUknes\nNwiZNRqbhnftF2+45wSF2bIJAemqGEhZmjcFLZuN6Myz8v/y8TOW2EhIQWgKyUYO\ns/xTGqi0nwiveJBUcgy+SbQT6LeMrI082QZqrkoP9UPsUpqwrChxRB8oKMWAqeM+\nKyydaT6ME/Di15uMUZ4wL/M8ldklKZbNDuflFTz/wuM6lnTMu8O1+YXwZBxtqAv+\n0bJAsWjcgs4diUYYUCeP9v+GvGAytQSr4VW4HD2VE10rBszZM14evOOS0M8/+//i\n+OKGAG8JuqMjfjWS1OEbtnWZcGjekTs/YVLSq01YxNBDptTo10oDVBvGK+DBh8t7\nKcu8MzzQuGGjjviM4ne+7M+eENb/BOtaukLIF6vWgeeJ5H+vMlb1U7jd1F9z2fcp\nb+NrEXI1iWJ3p2kc0vOn\n=pvcP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ef26963ebfb99faf130fabb512e1569ee79e4ee4\nparent 2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1783627888 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783627888 -0700\n\ncode-mode: fix installation on darwin (#31876)\n\nInstaller needs to symlink code-mode-host next to codex on install.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T20:11:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22781d40019779abc158723f2387cc6bce22a7ce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22781d40019779abc158723f2387cc6bce22a7ce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22781d40019779abc158723f2387cc6bce22a7ce/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f"}]},{"sha":"2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlOGMzNzU2Zjk1Nzg5YzIxNWQ5ZWE5YTVhZGU2ZWMzNzc5MzRiM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T18:53:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T18:53:18Z"},"message":"build: ratchet direct reqwest dependencies (#31431)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `codex-http-client` migration now has a shared implementation and\nseveral migrated request paths, but nothing prevents a new crate from\nadding another direct `reqwest` dependency while the remaining call\nsites are being converted. The dependency graph should both enforce the\ndirection of travel and make the remaining scope visible.\n\nThis PR adds that ratchet on top of #31363. It does not claim the\nmigration is complete: the allowlist deliberately records all 18\nfirst-party crates that still depend on `reqwest` directly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Ban `reqwest` with cargo-deny unless its immediate parent is an\nexplicitly listed wrapper.\n- Identify `codex-http-client` as the intended owner.\n- Record the 18 current first-party direct dependents as temporary\nmigration exceptions.\n- Separately allow six third-party integrations that own their `reqwest`\ndependency: `oauth2`, `opentelemetry-http`, `opentelemetry-otlp`,\n`rmcp`, `sentry`, and `webrtc-sys-build`.\n- Cover both `reqwest` 0.12 and 0.13 with the same package-level rule.\n\n## Migration rule\n\nA new first-party crate cannot add `reqwest`. When a listed crate\nfinishes migrating, its direct Cargo dependency and its wrapper entry\nshould be removed in the same PR, so the first-party list can only\nshrink.\n\n## Review guide\n\nThe entire change is the new `reqwest` entry in `codex-rs/deny.toml`:\n\n1. `codex-http-client` is the permanent intended wrapper.\n2. The next 18 entries are the first-party migration backlog.\n3. The final six entries are separately documented third-party parents\nrequired by cargo-deny graph semantics.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo deny check bans --hide-inclusion-graph` (`bans ok`; existing\nduplicate-version warnings remain warnings)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31431).\n* #31837\n* #31828\n* #31825\n* #31821\n* #31637\n* __->__ #31431","tree":{"sha":"493443274aa2f65fb6418661a2ce377cf741672f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/493443274aa2f65fb6418661a2ce377cf741672f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT+4eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyzAQAETC6TTpD6TD5ldtCJ7tl+WQ\n6C4cDjanAe1en0eSP69nZe8SaVYHcdboZKjzWzZMVzSuNQuNQizmFavEYq3yxl+3\nKQ+whTzc17edYBip+VDUoQ2n9DVwUlDm+p2tquhSoaJd2oPFliDFNHxzl8OCntqU\naiG/fAjKa0CoPR/omSFSh8SGJoKU4Ead+lPSN9ysa62Wm+rfTMgUOVimgggYPt+g\n9IxEYXMNaayyDLZTpThLia4bj5VICbHYU/mUFKv6vI7aKnFHKSY0ElxTyHbJ9WmS\nROQgc2bUnQLg9Z7f48cQWk/z6NL7337swtPSIc7A0wD8LEQu+ehVtsXL6q4BXBgm\nU6GJJkfTsHTlprTfS24nESfobqqWx7lIR+Tgo256tUJNCbYduGUa52B8KFHQOe8j\nk4B2NSbFmJ29Hy4yAvYKuylVisZvrXeHMU/16/NzxEIrG3eT5+zJZ1//DKTTmq5m\nomPMwd/JZRgaZ3xVQ95sJiaz6SQ5OpsALbnK5OlMr3+7rHalxkN4hllaTQQLrCAE\ntV9ZB8Z4S1mAIVSbxANMap/JZNdb53sXlhGEDkAB2NdbqGj17BA1hYehaK+/nIco\nlTBOvWzYte8wWMraCj1KZjwhgGKsnI5KYE/y0m6PgHhRG7KPp71wZqPs8/Rdnfv4\ndcr9WWfyGw5/67PsBLi6\n=6j7L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 493443274aa2f65fb6418661a2ce377cf741672f\nparent 2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1783623198 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783623198 -0700\n\nbuild: ratchet direct reqwest dependencies (#31431)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `codex-http-client` migration now has a shared implementation and\nseveral migrated request paths, but nothing prevents a new crate from\nadding another direct `reqwest` dependency while the remaining call\nsites are being converted. The dependency graph should both enforce the\ndirection of travel and make the remaining scope visible.\n\nThis PR adds that ratchet on top of #31363. It does not claim the\nmigration is complete: the allowlist deliberately records all 18\nfirst-party crates that still depend on `reqwest` directly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Ban `reqwest` with cargo-deny unless its immediate parent is an\nexplicitly listed wrapper.\n- Identify `codex-http-client` as the intended owner.\n- Record the 18 current first-party direct dependents as temporary\nmigration exceptions.\n- Separately allow six third-party integrations that own their `reqwest`\ndependency: `oauth2`, `opentelemetry-http`, `opentelemetry-otlp`,\n`rmcp`, `sentry`, and `webrtc-sys-build`.\n- Cover both `reqwest` 0.12 and 0.13 with the same package-level rule.\n\n## Migration rule\n\nA new first-party crate cannot add `reqwest`. When a listed crate\nfinishes migrating, its direct Cargo dependency and its wrapper entry\nshould be removed in the same PR, so the first-party list can only\nshrink.\n\n## Review guide\n\nThe entire change is the new `reqwest` entry in `codex-rs/deny.toml`:\n\n1. `codex-http-client` is the permanent intended wrapper.\n2. The next 18 entries are the first-party migration backlog.\n3. The final six entries are separately documented third-party parents\nrequired by cargo-deny graph semantics.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo deny check bans --hide-inclusion-graph` (`bans ok`; existing\nduplicate-version warnings remain warnings)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31431).\n* #31837\n* #31828\n* #31825\n* #31821\n* #31637\n* __->__ #31431","verified_at":"2026-07-09T18:53:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e8c3756f95789c215d9ea9a5ade6ec377934b3f/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372"}]},{"sha":"2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJjODU5NzVlZWFkMjQyOGFmNWI5NzdhMDQ4YTk4ODc1ZGVmNmIzNzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T18:36:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T18:36:36Z"},"message":"fix(sandboxing): initialize network proxy config inline (#31830)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #31767 flattened `NetworkProxyConfig`, leaving the [seatbelt test\nsetup](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91/codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_tests.rs#L660-L662)\nto assign fields directly after `NetworkProxyConfig::default()`. Rust\n1.95 flags that pattern as `clippy::field_reassign_with_default`, and\nthe macOS Bazel Clippy job treats the warning as an error, blocking\n`main` and PRs based on it.\n\n## What Changed\n\nInitialize `enabled` and `mode` in the `NetworkProxyConfig` struct\nliteral, then apply the Unix socket allowlist through the existing\nsetter. This preserves the test behavior while satisfying Clippy.\n\n## How to Test\n\nThis is a test-only initialization change, so there is no manual product\nflow.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-sandboxing` (65 passed)\n- `just clippy -p codex-sandboxing`\n\nThe local argument-comment lint could not complete because Bazel's LLVM\nrepository is missing the `compiler-rt` BUILD package. The touched Rust\ndiff was manually audited and adds no positional literal calls.","tree":{"sha":"027b19513a6b1d14037b6c4733adb7474cff467c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/027b19513a6b1d14037b6c4733adb7474cff467c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT+o0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGQUQADt7g/zliZrJnPDVjDq7Pcyx\nGHBVAf7X1adQjQQmd3NyrOznEmyj9x/rLnIBWDccaQfInuRFEvFxDhX54T+gaRlg\nuSXWlDPn395a7qLi7+kplrwE8O2d5cy3h1fmQAkaO24IbjnBM/EozE1q/PA9daik\nfGCsok8AZ1BlDXVOy1f5knpoaNjZLT59AajJtuyoigDxeo1cs+T8TX2739hLBP1M\nsq0JmxOaSbKuGe7MsMEWiXfND0Q7TnhOP8/lw6eR023G9XkkLq6OnNUs6Qck9959\nijM5LZb/etduuqJZUJnbT/x+4kpuuOXRf+oZdaU28Xq+I+BKN24F30VlU/6cY6DM\n/uhjPukJ27Aa/sbDweNkyrgR7uzHBeFreYL1tEFVLrc9vChwbckrxQbJ0ATEzKCN\nCU8j+8O0GgU1EXs2w5SAggQOaIu95fmXvXEFi4tR5mkjqX3PA7k5W+9+bhrNzM4n\nMljI4qwQQYlTcPQbtKwlyR8Pg6HLLkMqLnVqGHpLb2qdToB5kp2N3qYpfAJQ/HDa\nXF+nRsS4o3WkedOigt0yHpSQ8ZmGIRimiaLMH5OMioxo1eVUuAwifdSQWEw8xAGf\nMnjXEStGQLNkww9TI0eS+FCcu91CO+eybxea/MGkyNi2bJQPmoJBn/MqkSKgk3lz\ns48RUaC0dykAs3weoXZI\n=Pfo7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 027b19513a6b1d14037b6c4733adb7474cff467c\nparent d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1783622196 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783622196 +0100\n\nfix(sandboxing): initialize network proxy config inline (#31830)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #31767 flattened `NetworkProxyConfig`, leaving the [seatbelt test\nsetup](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91/codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_tests.rs#L660-L662)\nto assign fields directly after `NetworkProxyConfig::default()`. Rust\n1.95 flags that pattern as `clippy::field_reassign_with_default`, and\nthe macOS Bazel Clippy job treats the warning as an error, blocking\n`main` and PRs based on it.\n\n## What Changed\n\nInitialize `enabled` and `mode` in the `NetworkProxyConfig` struct\nliteral, then apply the Unix socket allowlist through the existing\nsetter. This preserves the test behavior while satisfying Clippy.\n\n## How to Test\n\nThis is a test-only initialization change, so there is no manual product\nflow.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-sandboxing` (65 passed)\n- `just clippy -p codex-sandboxing`\n\nThe local argument-comment lint could not complete because Bazel's LLVM\nrepository is missing the `compiler-rt` BUILD package. The touched Rust\ndiff was manually audited and adds no positional literal calls.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T18:36:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2c85975eead2428af5b977a048a98875def6b372/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91"}]},{"sha":"d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ3MmQ2NjljYTcyN2EyNjc2NTMxNWZmZTAzZGIzZGQyNTk0ZDliOTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T17:03:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T17:03:22Z"},"message":"tui: update safety buffering copy (#31813)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe safety-buffering message currently leads with additional safety\nchecks, which can make the delay feel accusatory. Update it to describe\nthe system taking more time before responding, matching the revised\nuser-facing language.\n\n- Replace the safety-buffering copy in both retry and non-retry flows.\n- Keep the faster-model escape hatch while aligning its wording with the\nupdated message.\n- Update the TUI snapshots for both states.","tree":{"sha":"5b53bb254424f1a1db76a443d3d2360be9e8f7b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5b53bb254424f1a1db76a443d3d2360be9e8f7b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT9RaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACQgQADegV2aUC7/HLVRn+UJ4Ot92\nfo6x/Er3VNNHqxcT4NPHS2kI3jvjwJ78OiYv/bDt7BnBwuKEDt2w1GLGoLOMo9Qc\nHPwFFxmioMQkhQXi34q+UJ3G5lD0A3DhizkLSEINodQlW78/J0tRVII5YflEOiHE\nZ6Py/PAcG6vFt7w9fo59lqh2gs7fyLlP2M4AOw3jUC5Q3NKkXDhjO4iQy23V+eYf\nAWS3jowVAu7fhm8Zi08frmrpmptTnLcTlSt610AWz0ovbX9PKimNcmB9z+LR+pED\ng97SavzPJ5dkRt+uP/PkN7vTJiw3q57QugDUfcFwekZ2SXzPON+UurO9G9btEIJx\nl1QDSH2UuZydHfit73WEZFbQiOXEatX5ReMpZybMyW0SVmwRYTpmiuGkZee/jUy8\n5j8SeH57+vSboWk9IKf0U9fbtwIGem6w65TmDXwwdzWTjvge9l6w/aA1bKZ8B6bf\nyepUyu6IGduzg1Y2Tp2Dz6G+7YZbR3ixqIViADuXEODignR65EJPYglaoAI3Tpuc\nbI5ZI5Dl5+cXEDdAWLYv6qZ8hZZEHnPA7buXpQZrkZiArEFEQ7O7bPRHt9KjhcPY\nCD5GPadTWilyM02qtnHRHw7SPAuZ/sy3IikzdHrr9JmUPohyBpIVTThR9tcFgYhZ\ncwRPgKnIW1Xe97OyWjZX\n=SyNw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5b53bb254424f1a1db76a443d3d2360be9e8f7b0\nparent 0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1783616602 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783616602 -0700\n\ntui: update safety buffering copy (#31813)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe safety-buffering message currently leads with additional safety\nchecks, which can make the delay feel accusatory. Update it to describe\nthe system taking more time before responding, matching the revised\nuser-facing language.\n\n- Replace the safety-buffering copy in both retry and non-retry flows.\n- Keep the faster-model escape hatch while aligning its wording with the\nupdated message.\n- Update the TUI snapshots for both states.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T17:03:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d72d669ca727a26765315ffe03db3dd2594d9b91/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b"}]},{"sha":"0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBlMTlkNWU5MDgzN2VkNjBhNWJkZTUzNDZmMjNhZDA4NWQzZmVhM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:58:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:58:22Z"},"message":"codex-api: route file uploads through HTTP client factory (#31363)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps file parameters use a three-step upload flow: create a file\nrecord, PUT bytes to a returned signed URL, and finalize the upload.\nEach step still constructed a default `reqwest` client, so the flow\ncould bypass `features.respect_system_proxy` even after model API\nrequests honored it.\n\nThis stack entry makes the resolved client policy a required input to\nthe upload API and resolves each concrete destination independently.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require `HttpClientFactory` in `upload_openai_file`.\n- Build clients for the create, signed upload, and finalize URLs through\nthe shared API route policy.\n- Pass the factory derived from the turn configuration at the Apps/MCP\ncall site.\n- Return a destination-aware `ClientBuild` error when enabled route\nselection cannot construct a client.\n- Preserve the legacy logged fallback for the feature-off\n`ReqwestDefault` policy.\n\n## Review guide\n\n1. `codex-api/src/files.rs` changes the upload API and centralizes\nroute-aware client construction.\n2. The three request stages each supply their actual URL, including the\nseparately hosted signed blob URL.\n3. `core/src/mcp_openai_file.rs` is the only production caller and\nsupplies the turn configuration factory.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p codex-api -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-api files` (1 matching upload test passed; 135\ntests skipped by filter)\n- `just fix -p codex-api -p codex-core`\n\n## Follow-up\n\nOther direct HTTP clients remain separate migration slices.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31363).\n* #31637\n* #31431\n* __->__ #31363","tree":{"sha":"f63571c347b402334ba32d3085f7a30c4a57f931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f63571c347b402334ba32d3085f7a30c4a57f931"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT9MuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATYgQAFsX9zFPc4Fc3+pW5g9Ya+em\ntVOBsuJQWBaksYz9SJJFmQe9tcRs/LKqgSOWxwi8vGXvMcAULHYo91glxAvsd2kg\nt+9RrcUOJUZpfMB9zha4zEBM0Kx/cozmsKUVoX1rV0XFF9+heKogPwXB1wTUJ5UE\nzPdZg14dXD00s1LsTasEZXYpYZ9tGear2kjlrEaCWiKR0szG28BWAGGrRAIXDrhh\nBX3D4CGopi7T1HNg0k6P8RDtisLnZmKQVcZ1TMqHTw17jmZAOALgn2tCLZgsk5xV\nmIjlhGTbphy/1R2JRM1wAfDnECDpKyrhFwTuZHLoKve/lWfylo9S8Wzt3oddYaRN\nH8BuiCk7CUnF0COlhsY95JcJsejS6JzvABNuGSViO20Vo6alZP3FIFgp5FCRBjyR\nmEeSGPmM48uDcNQ5GsRrDawWwDfBb4yXqVBBnQXRgFj8fBoZWPEPSJcvTN7q/PuA\nElWQMzMD1gtAkFKnwQE0BYVYFLsP/e3XdF0ZfFP+VlRiwCJb/heIyY/ZuolrXb8/\n/jZNKExw2UqJQWa9+Q5h5WpIMWG4MKd52jkmDEwZCxDv5sgfaHZC8n/upKQfHOhD\nN7uPG57kxUuPjpws4Jm/QxS9YmXq0HmrBFAaXpxwqGscf6ylcgiy5oHmmXQtbkwG\nymrdrssMqPVcI9m5d8/L\n=P9ei\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f63571c347b402334ba32d3085f7a30c4a57f931\nparent b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1783616302 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783616302 -0700\n\ncodex-api: route file uploads through HTTP client factory (#31363)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps file parameters use a three-step upload flow: create a file\nrecord, PUT bytes to a returned signed URL, and finalize the upload.\nEach step still constructed a default `reqwest` client, so the flow\ncould bypass `features.respect_system_proxy` even after model API\nrequests honored it.\n\nThis stack entry makes the resolved client policy a required input to\nthe upload API and resolves each concrete destination independently.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require `HttpClientFactory` in `upload_openai_file`.\n- Build clients for the create, signed upload, and finalize URLs through\nthe shared API route policy.\n- Pass the factory derived from the turn configuration at the Apps/MCP\ncall site.\n- Return a destination-aware `ClientBuild` error when enabled route\nselection cannot construct a client.\n- Preserve the legacy logged fallback for the feature-off\n`ReqwestDefault` policy.\n\n## Review guide\n\n1. `codex-api/src/files.rs` changes the upload API and centralizes\nroute-aware client construction.\n2. The three request stages each supply their actual URL, including the\nseparately hosted signed blob URL.\n3. `core/src/mcp_openai_file.rs` is the only production caller and\nsupplies the turn configuration factory.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p codex-api -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-api files` (1 matching upload test passed; 135\ntests skipped by filter)\n- `just fix -p codex-api -p codex-core`\n\n## Follow-up\n\nOther direct HTTP clients remain separate migration slices.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31363).\n* #31637\n* #31431\n* __->__ #31363","verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:58:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0e19d5e90837ed60a5bde5346f23ad085d3fea3b/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c"}]},{"sha":"b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI1ODk1MmIwZmE4ODlmNzk1OGFmMzdkMDU3YjUyMWYzZmRhYjRkM2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"raquel-openai","email":"raquel@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:51:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:51:44Z"},"message":"fix: forward originator to Codex Apps MCP (#31481)\n\n## Summary\n- Forward Codexs canonical `originator` header on ChatGPT-hosted Apps\nand plugin-runtime MCP requests.\n- Preserve the configured `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku` header.\n- Cover originator-only and originator-plus-SKU configurations.\n\n## Why\nSites project creation is logged downstream of Apps MCP. Production\nvalidation found `CODEX_UNKNOWN_DEFAULT` project-created threads that\nmatched `codex_surface=desktop_app` and `originator=Codex Desktop` in\n`fact_codex_cli`\n([query](https://kepler.gateway.data-1.internal.api.openai.org/permalink/H_mVoVPqLQ0)).\n\nThe hosted Apps MCP configuration forwarded the product SKU but not\nCodexs canonical originator, so codex-backend could not derive\n`CODEX_DESKTOP_APP` for those tool calls.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `CARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-cargo-home\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-target just test -p codex-mcp` (106\npassed)\n- `CARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-cargo-home\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-target just fix -p codex-mcp`","tree":{"sha":"59bd826877e48da7c556e565b74791ba1c5ea784","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/59bd826877e48da7c556e565b74791ba1c5ea784"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT9GgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2SsQABFPSYoGD8dU29RCPYc/F/WA\nivKEtkKo7gY6PsDP1kVDNEeqn2brD2CiAYqIOktU+ospRmB2QJSeuD6YhZttpJ3h\nXrhARaXy0u0LlPXUbAP6873phjnp0xSv04JCbLhtnZCoBHYib25kUWI1T7HDW/5n\n7TWsds3T0vTmr9DVmNs/430JCoi/saAg0DQsvwtCw6PpAxVBysLRSdVePWmZrpvm\nmaFEkZF2SB1+o04PJogbwttn37xLBwECnWEtJNIcSkpFotb8Lv8k0ELT/3Tr/yEO\nnir0ulOaEJMM3pX3hflBIsZRmGNr6Ni08n0fFUiPKy0vXDvNhmYav3OHArpmie4l\nnk73c6W72u9lYdNDHcXYnbEZ2iudWd/cVEbARGRZBrzeh7YFqabnz/k8MsTLMrt4\nx2f/OnYBcWpzqVBGgVXBZedLnka/zyIku625m3ON3wIgFQI4xjZTGf6OhqwwmBg1\nK6A+5kmflY5/ejCPRD8S/ee9RZD1mweylkOnZtI59vZrgGkz6kM03iPYzVxVP9fs\nibRhaZCN+3eaSjUmSm1gwf26gN5jlt7Q4PNrd2X2tT/k3tGNtVfMSgyFmQXUgmQ6\nuk2Sl6JmBNUfLqR9LrpztREbm3bNJLYY1rs8lQk5T90o3KFXRGDx3VHfFB8vGPXo\nXQlZbEFongfWQrfe7BeP\n=0imn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59bd826877e48da7c556e565b74791ba1c5ea784\nparent cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d\nauthor raquel-openai <raquel@openai.com> 1783615904 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783615904 +0000\n\nfix: forward originator to Codex Apps MCP (#31481)\n\n## Summary\n- Forward Codexs canonical `originator` header on ChatGPT-hosted Apps\nand plugin-runtime MCP requests.\n- Preserve the configured `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku` header.\n- Cover originator-only and originator-plus-SKU configurations.\n\n## Why\nSites project creation is logged downstream of Apps MCP. Production\nvalidation found `CODEX_UNKNOWN_DEFAULT` project-created threads that\nmatched `codex_surface=desktop_app` and `originator=Codex Desktop` in\n`fact_codex_cli`\n([query](https://kepler.gateway.data-1.internal.api.openai.org/permalink/H_mVoVPqLQ0)).\n\nThe hosted Apps MCP configuration forwarded the product SKU but not\nCodexs canonical originator, so codex-backend could not derive\n`CODEX_DESKTOP_APP` for those tool calls.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `CARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-cargo-home\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-target just test -p codex-mcp` (106\npassed)\n- `CARGO_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-cargo-home\nCARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-target just fix -p codex-mcp`","verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:51:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b58952b0fa889f7958af37d057b521f3fdab4d3c/comments","author":{"login":"raquel-openai","id":190536808,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1tcaA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190536808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/raquel-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raquel-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d"}]},{"sha":"cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNmNmQ4YWQ5MjExYmE4ZmE2ZjgyMDBkMmRkYjI1M2ExYWQxNTJmN2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:33:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:33:37Z"},"message":"Remove the network proxy config wrapper (#31767)\n\n## Why\n\n`NetworkProxyConfig` only wrapped `NetworkProxySettings` in a single\n`network` field. That extra level made runtime callers repeat `.network`\neverywhere without representing a real boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- move the managed-network fields directly onto `NetworkProxyConfig`\n- collapse the matching partial-config wrapper\n- update runtime callers and tests to use the direct fields\n- keep the user-facing permissions/profile TOML layout unchanged\n\nThe internal serialized shape now matches the runtime type itself. This\ndoes not change managed-network behavior or the `config.toml` shape.","tree":{"sha":"9de6a356ea36ab80593361f6e0159d6044046009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9de6a356ea36ab80593361f6e0159d6044046009"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT81hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu4AQADSheoo8KbgUDN8nxMopy1z2\nU8QxbiJqY9cEE+FmGSdiWyJVuVOKWu96qsdc12vdPcrUroAbC10vGadU3ISydLca\n8U1vK8aQol9/Kzi1ATeHGEuOvNCAJmV1mmTcfvGo2gGLLDiNOaTUtx5L4dPjQevF\nwufNcOtnNQ4lHNwPK3N1eAy4cc0SKCFk6TB8y8E1ixysq5Q5T5VWcjmsi+EXp/5s\nORpr9xYrK0leSfhBbyUtOolgbZIuLQQijz9mhUjDXap9BcgqruFMUEMuaBS4ZnxM\nymhe+mFZ60RiTgysyR130nbHlws9J+wewvfE/eOlChuuD33XvBXfjtsVJ2YZU1Mv\ndOUfSulHPSY/KVIeXjIuyiZP7RDWNGoEqGbR7G6fh7QwJascnOuWmFAYBmUDnNl2\nqmJB1HTtwnD6470DDDCQPoAwAWhk7F6fkBqrf9ea4ICbdJirfmVcDZrVB/2ncBh+\nu2DIZ4TuaDqlwIjKaP6jx+IgXXqxj6h/9SYzkg41zhw42i6rrJrZ9iNRzMUO02uF\ndcMWCUMmP44H/00/wXUKfuicuEbnm3i10JrTHPrdp1pdslhfSRWikVk6+TVpIZ1G\nbpSD5REC4FrBbi9C4mDa3RzI+3oXeLkynEtHW8O2aCrNR5ZuRv9DnYRlrYy226dY\nJqVATS3w+jc1dn8o2K/b\n=8WT+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9de6a356ea36ab80593361f6e0159d6044046009\nparent f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783614817 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783614817 +0100\n\nRemove the network proxy config wrapper (#31767)\n\n## Why\n\n`NetworkProxyConfig` only wrapped `NetworkProxySettings` in a single\n`network` field. That extra level made runtime callers repeat `.network`\neverywhere without representing a real boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- move the managed-network fields directly onto `NetworkProxyConfig`\n- collapse the matching partial-config wrapper\n- update runtime callers and tests to use the direct fields\n- keep the user-facing permissions/profile TOML layout unchanged\n\nThe internal serialized shape now matches the runtime type itself. This\ndoes not change managed-network behavior or the `config.toml` shape.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:33:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf6d8ad9211ba8fa6f8200d2ddb253a1ad152f7d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3"}]},{"sha":"f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY0NmI1M2JkODVjMTBjMmFmYmQ0NGI4OTIyMTY0YzQ5ZDU4MmMyYzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:27:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:27:50Z"},"message":"fix(tui): hide empty reasoning summaries (#31652)\n\n## Why\n\nReasoning summaries can contain an empty HTML comment placeholder, `<!--\n-->`, when a generated summary part has no prose. The TUI treated that\nplaceholder as visible summary content, so it leaked into both the\ncompleted conversation history and persisted transcript. Multi-part\nempty summaries could also leave later generated status headings visible\nas orphaned transcript content.\n\n## What\n\n- Strip the empty reasoning-summary placeholder at the shared\n`ReasoningSummaryCell` boundary.\n- Suppress the cell when removing placeholders leaves only generated\nbold status headings.\n- Cover the multi-part placeholder-only shape with a rendering\nregression test for both normal history and transcript output.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex TUI with reasoning summaries visible, for example with\n`hide_agent_reasoning = false` and `model_reasoning_summary =\n\"detailed\"`.\n2. Run a turn that receives an empty generated reasoning-summary part.\n3. Confirm that the in-progress status heading may appear while the turn\nis running, but the completed history and transcript contain neither\nliteral `<!-- -->` tokens nor orphaned reasoning headings.\n4. Confirm that a reasoning summary with actual prose still renders\nnormally.\n\nThe model output is nondeterministic, so the targeted regression covers\nthe exact multi-part placeholder shape from the report:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nreasoning_summary_block_hides_empty_html_comment_parts`","tree":{"sha":"2996a488ee31ad5aff2c673656568b85d717afce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2996a488ee31ad5aff2c673656568b85d717afce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8wGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQUkQAAUBZYLvQEST8bO39SMQpk+m\nlE5mR4sYFP/d0mjHfMbRcoJabWppG+IV3iL0u+5QfGmKGKL3oWITXaD0Z+1aex/r\nXNj+luvEWu7WkCH/MM3J6ILKhKDXj0ij0iuKotPHNLl1MlqWJZMatFYVTFFzVQah\n3bec1SMJdmSCm5Ue+hF/Q4MsK5yt5xlaqJuKmes8REiAeU7mHtF7Y/Pb8YfCPmRX\nSyYkPDDberxcql4lkCrXoPfvCRUlum5mc+0J+R/Q7p1JhQi/sB3LStG/beQb/uRG\nnps3JRqR8J3WEdbSWFhQDC9PzBnKYxDIElbwbrm7UdudwkRe7lK4D6EwvV50cqKu\nGNm8MbR6h4BYmaNPlPMW/IYHrKSfLRVy6R0H3N0J/yuZRmEfvjmHKa3rz/15DclY\nbFX8+vfOUom3EQLIUErycTfb9WUrIxLZwBnCnHJkLOv5dTrL+1lq17p6AWtDbCOj\nlBuQZTYUlVci8yiRud4SEEOCYS4JXH7PgAyh2gR8xOLskhxqLmlEnsKb/3R+Qdu2\nH82cwlXq7m1f3PlruBDhUIByH72bJTLx7DhnL7bvig7RcGcV47lUDwH5+abQ0kFD\n4Dl/UeHTYuWKtM6bHXmxwxXk9sXB1lcOQDn3OnGe47rk8rUhu0LvmO9otPBH0CFA\nALgYdzAqQVWtizEDRVo4\n=STJJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2996a488ee31ad5aff2c673656568b85d717afce\nparent 8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1783614470 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783614470 +0000\n\nfix(tui): hide empty reasoning summaries (#31652)\n\n## Why\n\nReasoning summaries can contain an empty HTML comment placeholder, `<!--\n-->`, when a generated summary part has no prose. The TUI treated that\nplaceholder as visible summary content, so it leaked into both the\ncompleted conversation history and persisted transcript. Multi-part\nempty summaries could also leave later generated status headings visible\nas orphaned transcript content.\n\n## What\n\n- Strip the empty reasoning-summary placeholder at the shared\n`ReasoningSummaryCell` boundary.\n- Suppress the cell when removing placeholders leaves only generated\nbold status headings.\n- Cover the multi-part placeholder-only shape with a rendering\nregression test for both normal history and transcript output.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start Codex TUI with reasoning summaries visible, for example with\n`hide_agent_reasoning = false` and `model_reasoning_summary =\n\"detailed\"`.\n2. Run a turn that receives an empty generated reasoning-summary part.\n3. Confirm that the in-progress status heading may appear while the turn\nis running, but the completed history and transcript contain neither\nliteral `<!-- -->` tokens nor orphaned reasoning headings.\n4. Confirm that a reasoning summary with actual prose still renders\nnormally.\n\nThe model output is nondeterministic, so the targeted regression covers\nthe exact multi-part placeholder shape from the report:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nreasoning_summary_block_hides_empty_html_comment_parts`","verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:27:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f46b53bd85c10c2afbd44b8922164c49d582c2c3/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c"}]},{"sha":"8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkYzc3ZmFmNTE3MTlmZjQxODhhY2NmYWEzYWU5MTZjZjBlMjUzOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:16:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T16:16:15Z"},"message":"Import enabled plugins from known marketplaces (#31672)\n\n## Summary\n\n- discover enabled-plugin marketplace sources from the user-level known\nmarketplace registry\n- preserve scoped settings and supported Git/directory declarations,\nfalling back to the matching registry `installLocation` for file, URL,\nnpm-hosted, and inline marketplace sources\n- resolve relative registry materialization paths against the\nexternal-agent home\n- reuse the existing marketplace add and plugin install flow during\nimport\n- emit `plugin_not_found` tracing and analytics with plugin and\nmarketplace identity\n\n## Why\n\nEnabled plugins can remain in settings after their marketplace source\nhas moved into the user-level registry. Import detection previously\nskipped those plugins because it only consulted settings-defined\nmarketplace sources.\n\n## Impact\n\n`/import` can now restore those marketplaces and install their enabled\nplugins through the normal plugin installer, including npm, Git, and\nlocal plugin sources. Missing plugins remain visible in import results\nand the plugin-install failure analytics stream.","tree":{"sha":"f6f1623b6b8e3dcd64b0d522f7bf59dc274934a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f6f1623b6b8e3dcd64b0d522f7bf59dc274934a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT8lPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4iIQACZ5nhiA8xQRVSBzNR5vC9SF\n4wjMsP1zF6cvD4RdWXCQBgX4NMWnKK5b4Ch+egu9u/ZCFdqbLvIkvJY3j6nxOY7/\nvVa+Eo1iuZO0SxZHBaMLrvWiBjbBm285f56MK+fC0FaNKK4LR1CCiVr64epG1udm\n5alsVrynKohh21RnIh2fQ7gO9N00Z/9Uw+7JJWuVFYcJRML0hQa/042QE8HXxCuq\nTXoIMPg9XkqNUJCXXzDA5z/dxVpSmJhuacdqSvH6qJy7UqjqNjNHX5l6UfzxtNJo\nHsY+6PcUq21y8+VosVCV+7fzw8AXoQJYh4KrosnyNAFTeZaUOWmHuvokhCuY3DUP\nLrfI71W3nrwzQyOAuEaz+u1dkNlSEMJ6uZQCGa+Krvd47LjLVvzaXs8JMuD3dM0+\nyyHRC1rgh2vX2kqxMuTh1VDCuIWqZANbBxVFrPvhPSr1gpK8L3zq2owhikXWsZOe\nmdwfZcAzsuxsyMbfESdRFblj6Yl8mfDobuCeEyQNEw8nD6fbeULrBUvJxWQsog+1\nN5+DJ+N89gs1szGYLrNA3muW8bb08GZmPW/JlGDTsR5kXD60B+jIZeM+DOLIxkRv\nk9a+zAmCilYJE13LKB2l0Iu7wjrS/lNzgFLCDzCPY3YIABHjQ5i8PZFOU7ZB87JR\nuKKay8l5QQhUM+YZLxSp\n=evuj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f6f1623b6b8e3dcd64b0d522f7bf59dc274934a4\nparent a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1783613775 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783613775 -0400\n\nImport enabled plugins from known marketplaces (#31672)\n\n## Summary\n\n- discover enabled-plugin marketplace sources from the user-level known\nmarketplace registry\n- preserve scoped settings and supported Git/directory declarations,\nfalling back to the matching registry `installLocation` for file, URL,\nnpm-hosted, and inline marketplace sources\n- resolve relative registry materialization paths against the\nexternal-agent home\n- reuse the existing marketplace add and plugin install flow during\nimport\n- emit `plugin_not_found` tracing and analytics with plugin and\nmarketplace identity\n\n## Why\n\nEnabled plugins can remain in settings after their marketplace source\nhas moved into the user-level registry. Import detection previously\nskipped those plugins because it only consulted settings-defined\nmarketplace sources.\n\n## Impact\n\n`/import` can now restore those marketplaces and install their enabled\nplugins through the normal plugin installer, including npm, Git, and\nlocal plugin sources. Missing plugins remain visible in import results\nand the plugin-install failure analytics stream.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T16:16:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8dc77faf51719ff4188accfaa3ae916cf0e2539c/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9"}]},{"sha":"a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE2Yjk5ZWU1YzQ1ZTM1MTY1YzliYWM5ZGE0Y2VjNjVmMmNhNTViYzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T15:17:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T15:17:13Z"},"message":"code-mode: retain shared MCP types for deferred tools (#31745)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen MCP tools are deferred behind `tool_search`, Code mode keeps them\ncallable but omits their individual declarations from the initial `exec`\ndescription. The shared MCP `CallToolResult` types were derived only\nfrom directly rendered tools, so deferring every MCP tool also removed\nthe common response contract that models need to interpret MCP results.\n\nThis restores that contract without undoing the context savings from\ndeferred tool definitions. This is a follow-up to #29486.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Track deferred Code-mode tool definitions separately from directly\nrendered definitions.\n- Render the shared MCP type preamble when either direct or deferred MCP\ntools are available.\n- Keep deferred tool declarations out of the initial prompt.\n- Add unit and integration coverage for deferred MCP tools.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_only_guides_all_tools_search_and_calls_deferred_app_tools`","tree":{"sha":"4a206f07862f629c07de873b3c0b9b952f487d1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4a206f07862f629c07de873b3c0b9b952f487d1c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT7t5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0TsQAF9y76hLDygvLJaZ6PPHDYYr\ned7tLsg8j+Mvvlrp3Qsh/YoZGvCeKXK823KNA1BLR90XnlmJYqcpxlp+qNuXQOLp\n8R/rKdEPN1mint/5/173OaY2ZhGaSggcpZm79nrSUvCeE0iVeZccqIQP4wAgKiDz\nPcnaBs23E2o3V4dxP3Gcq1DCyyV1GG0IK9OL7dOaPh4HtmXoqtdcpkI8l37FrD2a\nrieQqIG1W7TKKeMDgWwp9R0zw0hZnLWaAIHSq0YwAIEAr4h0LfxMUY1AiTvy2hdI\nljE7U6Hmd86YoIAfyFLaPRpfjG1hMhytL6x98nXESuEkzXBWgxSCLf8E+NcAykX7\nU2Qj4+gg3TitpYoO9lTo7XfA9ISlYEzWn+Ktoq3UJwNT9SmlAEGRA4BCWXpxcDfs\ncQtWsz1A1C/e9Pr4VacUmmtrQqkUPZfuCOaQ/SBWW3wurOGv+MEQzZ98Csv12vyr\n7aqf3ulpTE2iWlpKh+n5qHv/sa6DjbYrJUGCQOeyuCC95cY48ZsUQQxWgXruKei1\nSdVxaFwVvUxAKx2gCimQGpupJynNUdsHame41+CxgKRywj/CBUTomiXlxNLVA3f5\nnHmBeQ9MsUcwOQUbbjqM6swSe4D23L5S4+d/vlOWDqYJGfZMt85VuYmaYtDuWPez\nZbRgqeIHTdXpVhTvgmiP\n=c4ND\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4a206f07862f629c07de873b3c0b9b952f487d1c\nparent 23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1783610233 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783610233 -0700\n\ncode-mode: retain shared MCP types for deferred tools (#31745)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen MCP tools are deferred behind `tool_search`, Code mode keeps them\ncallable but omits their individual declarations from the initial `exec`\ndescription. The shared MCP `CallToolResult` types were derived only\nfrom directly rendered tools, so deferring every MCP tool also removed\nthe common response contract that models need to interpret MCP results.\n\nThis restores that contract without undoing the context savings from\ndeferred tool definitions. This is a follow-up to #29486.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Track deferred Code-mode tool definitions separately from directly\nrendered definitions.\n- Render the shared MCP type preamble when either direct or deferred MCP\ntools are available.\n- Keep deferred tool declarations out of the initial prompt.\n- Add unit and integration coverage for deferred MCP tools.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-code-mode-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_only_guides_all_tools_search_and_calls_deferred_app_tools`","verified_at":"2026-07-09T15:17:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6b99ee5c45e35165c9bac9da4cec65f2ca55bc9/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1"}]},{"sha":"23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIzYTA5ZWIzYzNkMDBhYjJhMmI5NmI2OWFhODE0NTRhMGE4OGNjYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alec Barber","email":"ab@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T15:04:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T15:04:02Z"},"message":"fix(mcp): default Apps product SKU to codex (#31803)\n\n## Motivation\n\nHost-owned Apps MCP requests currently omit `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku`\nunless `apps_mcp_product_sku` is explicitly configured. Codex requests\nshould identify themselves with the `codex` product SKU by default.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Default `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku` to `codex`.\n- Preserve explicitly configured SKU values.\n- Add coverage for both default and configured behavior.\n\n## Impact\n\nCodex Apps MCP requests now include the expected product identity\nwithout requiring local configuration. Existing explicit SKU overrides\nare unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\ncodex_apps_server_config_sets_product_sku_header`\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"da8a4b38f9c493998bc8aafcb56b3fc5ef2808ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/da8a4b38f9c493998bc8aafcb56b3fc5ef2808ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT7hjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHdAQADoHMWHL6PBVtEj6hBuUvsjI\nsDJ2rknutQsO7V7i0nQ0haU2kuvpT2C+yX/glQv/hEEeZfRLes5ad75SGaABuXyl\nmOPpShG7+WSCogjwLQrzwue/cbWQzxFQQojd83EvcHX9yV7CAHjg7bvGBemzpfau\nahLz+Nw1ENDkFyOLT34j4BjVTn8zvqf6hN+L6XMAmSANmliQ9Uxw4AMGmUxLLB8A\n1I+CSKpbwrg8gBn4Jumrg5/adgxjOChZyuG/PkGU6j9WAuyyw8kjZNyovUJBaZEH\n6Ob6Y/aL64RTwfRpQ1pEELm3tI+qKUZcHLGJ/sLxjY8JZ5S1lMOwHTFc6fr2+Lwi\nkBc//o3fqMw9MYrHolhXnK8TBJSsRLQ8KuZ+BiKgIg9XdpZ5ngSnEBDVRE2Eick0\nx5RU2dD4dyhEQ0AbXEFUmE/N9eEtCwmcMz6JRzxZ/oDY9e3YFk0MG+fn+1zs6/91\ncZK7WZ84By4gJookcaNndv2BRzZ/yvRlDXKOMTSBeT2GTDXMVImCLbujFS4HfWuy\n/9JK3OacOlTwNFV5IjgTb+O+4B+MRtoJzKPhL1Osc2tDhqb2kNCmI0woQBfo5jFt\n+WrYTxBLN4vcFNsctpu2scJTz9mMywy2JXJoSzGqeGWwV6S+fh97ob8PQbQxvXvz\nkf4R/XsP9qA+9ICWzrTN\n=Oqv5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da8a4b38f9c493998bc8aafcb56b3fc5ef2808ae\nparent 091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40\nauthor Alec Barber <ab@openai.com> 1783609442 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783609442 +0100\n\nfix(mcp): default Apps product SKU to codex (#31803)\n\n## Motivation\n\nHost-owned Apps MCP requests currently omit `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku`\nunless `apps_mcp_product_sku` is explicitly configured. Codex requests\nshould identify themselves with the `codex` product SKU by default.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Default `X-OpenAI-Product-Sku` to `codex`.\n- Preserve explicitly configured SKU values.\n- Add coverage for both default and configured behavior.\n\n## Impact\n\nCodex Apps MCP requests now include the expected product identity\nwithout requiring local configuration. Existing explicit SKU overrides\nare unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp\ncodex_apps_server_config_sets_product_sku_header`\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-07-09T15:04:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/23a09eb3c3d00ab2a2b96b69aa81454a0a88cca1/comments","author":{"login":"alecbarber-oai","id":226170457,"node_id":"U_kgDODXsWWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/226170457?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alecbarber-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alecbarber-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40"}]},{"sha":"091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA5MWIyYWRhOTQ1ZTRlNzRjNGQyZDcwNzAxZDI5N2JjNzExNmZmNDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T14:44:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T14:44:59Z"},"message":"Stabilize the memories feature flag (#31804)\n\nMemories is graduating from the experimental lifecycle, but it should\nremain opt-in.\n\nThis changes the feature stage to stable while keeping `default_enabled`\nfalse. It removes memories from the experimental menu and announcement\nwithout enabling it by default.\n\nCompanion Codex Apps PR: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1110434","tree":{"sha":"c4f20b5799594e2c351e8afaf0ce2849c96e87aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c4f20b5799594e2c351e8afaf0ce2849c96e87aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT7PrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAomoQAKdpwEGlOuUw66DyEu71Mwow\nqrWl1e4sWozpqZxQIz5JMi2g7gy4bL3HedW3a+QZ7QYsEbOwrgmRF+5R9qbh8buK\nYISRZeR5Uuxfcbj6Sdfb+Cph8xSKq/lyt2fEN4epzFw4c8m+ASwwJ2IBQl0oYeD8\niTmU+T4qJIQtZbW1N9mhQBBvsxwpcoIGWv/e9mZ4eAniwRjvDu2xMMepBFYkVgcT\np4bZdpJLNz/UaTASKLn12dLOmiEkdc5rHxakiaEQxq83TT9ndrC3GoDVmiuqt9i6\nThpRFGJdcZyrNgf69zA5OhUOy1IyD16nzVlhVHVjynXyohem5m9apyU2RADyjr1f\nLRyKpVSwp3dY3TdFM6yfScpuzLh32V6GKEYJ/u9xPax8z1ycatYT5rSZ7CoWdJiW\nX0ysmUNVKhHMEKB4qSWaDjh1lJYlPBQINaKs/Z5+5wyiJ20RWoNmWtquWhMY3Rd9\n0NzbJkwyFBKynJLm7De5zYV+ta57SXJIwmFKYoHnCHjiyzYGkkYmk53A3KXIjCsH\nk6Z7969z23ADKmfgbucbKdaWmf+iKZ5fnnahmLAUaQey+LLXCnSXYGYS2vWR2sJk\nkF4TJU+uVjA6zKR/mOenKgrFMEt9i+lwzcH6wYHyyHVcD6w1v8A6VlYzXcohPjSu\nfDBZ3FtDEuy5YFFRmS4a\n=HRyH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c4f20b5799594e2c351e8afaf0ce2849c96e87aa\nparent c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783608299 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783608299 +0100\n\nStabilize the memories feature flag (#31804)\n\nMemories is graduating from the experimental lifecycle, but it should\nremain opt-in.\n\nThis changes the feature stage to stable while keeping `default_enabled`\nfalse. It removes memories from the experimental menu and announcement\nwithout enabling it by default.\n\nCompanion Codex Apps PR: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1110434","verified_at":"2026-07-09T14:44:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/091b2ada945e4e74c4d2d70701d297bc7116ff40/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755"}]},{"sha":"c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM4ZDJkYjljYzA2ZjZkOTcyNzU3OTczYTkyMjRlZWFlZmI1NmM3NTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:36:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:36:15Z"},"message":"Reduce MCP tool-list trace volume (#31790)\n\n## Why\n\nEvery MCP tool-list build emitted two normal-path TRACE events per\nconfigured server: one before waiting for tools and one after listing\nthem. On active sessions this produced thousands of nearly identical\nSQLite rows while carrying little information beyond server readiness\nand tool counts.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove the two normal-path per-server TRACE events.\n- Keep the existing per-server trace span for timing and remote trace\ncontext.\n- Emit per-server details only when a server's tools are unavailable.\n- Emit one bounded summary per tool-list build with available server,\nunavailable server, and tool counts.\n\nSuccessful builds retain the useful aggregate signal without repeating\nit for every server.\n\nRelated to #28224.","tree":{"sha":"6998f474f9478396e5360be3c46c631a5c4f64ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6998f474f9478396e5360be3c46c631a5c4f64ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6PPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMVkQADgo/1NybayofbmnBKfHYzCv\ngNfILpdCzHLLE8e1G68FDbylMF0Fw2Qy7Yz9f7hA7InqJPSm6ogo4mNeUjzuT739\naJdQwZk1Dfdi40dbeQodaPD5S36v31uwUbdCNOQQ/1J4OjQz9Sxcc4GxvrsNH+1a\nkRUBV+dpjWz7VAG6fA0vnf32mG5RunVJLW9WKZRzvmvN0knkS4hsjwCqkrPL/6xd\nqkSgjLz5SYwHApBJqDyeMpHve+WX1hyF8cLNQ9Es/wm/qBjLAjLO96imbwi1AN6g\ngvsap3a2e/kk8VsHgokcpQYfV/vImLjDD45SIsupP4f4Z0znPgZUFY4EFc2NfuVI\nXpfiP5Y0pkrfOoOTy882oDVw5oU4q/b4f9i2Ezr883uzQi+QvusQylvOmXD3L53y\nt4rwcIaCf1RmM4MQSr4C4mm592Dsub3SrK4yDErw8h3sRQHNjcRk6SHp6aU89sGl\nGG58WnTCHICz3073yN5jBpDWswZcs/ppwBjn1hkQTY9O2zWPwIA0NaNo7Is5odac\nXp1coy6evmsPgUymzZ8PoFk1WZJyzLM46gJ01ktKeBZMX61QmlubUqUOFbPZEctp\nKDWE+d3ASEA7J8NqZkf7cXyO3itNyVoSRSnZtCTuHADdwF0VbwJXQKVcoighee2S\nAAPpUkZDaQdIx3peO35s\n=L7rZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6998f474f9478396e5360be3c46c631a5c4f64ca\nparent bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783604175 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604175 +0100\n\nReduce MCP tool-list trace volume (#31790)\n\n## Why\n\nEvery MCP tool-list build emitted two normal-path TRACE events per\nconfigured server: one before waiting for tools and one after listing\nthem. On active sessions this produced thousands of nearly identical\nSQLite rows while carrying little information beyond server readiness\nand tool counts.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove the two normal-path per-server TRACE events.\n- Keep the existing per-server trace span for timing and remote trace\ncontext.\n- Emit per-server details only when a server's tools are unavailable.\n- Emit one bounded summary per tool-list build with available server,\nunavailable server, and tool counts.\n\nSuccessful builds retain the useful aggregate signal without repeating\nit for every server.\n\nRelated to #28224.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T13:36:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8d2db9cc06f6d972757973a9224eeaefb56c755/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb"}]},{"sha":"bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJmYTNlZWI4YmZlZDhkMWJiZjExNDIzNjAwNzg3ZTA1Y2Y3ZWI4ZWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:35:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:35:09Z"},"message":"Filter routine Hyper logs from SQLite (#31791)\n\n## Why\n\nThe SQLite feedback log currently persists Hyper's TRACE, DEBUG, and\nINFO connection-pool bookkeeping. Healthy connects, checkouts, reuse,\nand timer activity generated thousands of small rows during active\nsessions without adding useful feedback context.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Set the `hyper_util` target prefix to WARN for the SQLite feedback-log\nlayer.\n- Continue persisting Hyper warnings and errors.\n- Leave other tracing and OpenTelemetry subscribers unchanged.\n\nThis removes routine dependency chatter while preserving actionable\nfailures.\n\nRelated to #28224.","tree":{"sha":"57b85bd01b7d4ed3751f4017ffbaa37cf9c93795","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/57b85bd01b7d4ed3751f4017ffbaa37cf9c93795"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6ONCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA07QQADB8WHRwKfLkE1nDUpBRohni\nh6iVImQ2lmF+aZOTtJwIcVmj2b5mMZ6VNA8bQkZgqbBRRJsgWKudNG80kQtJxBS4\nsNMLrzsY0J2u5YetcJQQ86M+g4jJJV+7zKsdwzAfu5SIPC4elF4CROBD6fQAVjpK\n5eg9i6YG0uMcFmlFvMjvOgAfmBMQJui13SWRSmouByqbjSMlsoBQa9gB3pZGvjJm\nPtbEX+a6QUHH9XDq9u+0EkeK6FTsKnYLDdUnFGI1+oWbIC+RDoW5+HookjeOISjG\nUddB9I22I4AjKgWaSsxYyV3yUro+nztsVW2xOgYBtl8uH2pkjEud86wj2jwiDMJs\nANSo4gQ/PrRio2oGa/gtAkg58ZcJUPY+yfBVr4LYbk01YgICFNWoikNIz41/T0ix\nexCsSaTptvqHDeYzoeUrDw/tH8baPc0tYOauDb88iVHats5CMyFVRXAKaOnzMjEV\nG6Z+M1703nxFo6rA5jPSfQ4XsIIuQGwvTq8bZuUaFH4u/o33A40MBDAXAgFegHQG\nkzys5h1w85r5zq6XaQWHPaQiNlxff3HFgUWGnlqUxSczN7u4FNlP2uEBk9/tdYrj\nJ6HZkZG5cBYQux4ozCswpnE+RwCAy8OUUlSMlOt0ieYp/yFduOBY2LlJAYX06/Um\nbMxhOhpiPePvUblxQzJ/\n=i6jv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57b85bd01b7d4ed3751f4017ffbaa37cf9c93795\nparent 538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783604109 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604109 +0100\n\nFilter routine Hyper logs from SQLite (#31791)\n\n## Why\n\nThe SQLite feedback log currently persists Hyper's TRACE, DEBUG, and\nINFO connection-pool bookkeeping. Healthy connects, checkouts, reuse,\nand timer activity generated thousands of small rows during active\nsessions without adding useful feedback context.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Set the `hyper_util` target prefix to WARN for the SQLite feedback-log\nlayer.\n- Continue persisting Hyper warnings and errors.\n- Leave other tracing and OpenTelemetry subscribers unchanged.\n\nThis removes routine dependency chatter while preserving actionable\nfailures.\n\nRelated to #28224.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T13:35:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bfa3eeb8bfed8d1bbf11423600787e05cf7eb8eb/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e"}]},{"sha":"538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUzOGYyOWVkNWRhMGQxNjExNDE3MTQ4NzY5YTE3OTkxNzJiYjgzMGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:35:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:35:02Z"},"message":"Summarize streamed response item logs (#31792)\n\n## Why\n\n`handle_non_tool_response_item` logged the complete decoded\n`ResponseItem` at DEBUG. Those values can contain assistant text,\nreasoning content, and tool payloads that are already stored in the\ndurable rollout, making the SQLite copy both redundant and potentially\nlarge or sensitive.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the complete item dump with bounded `item_type` and `item_id`\nfields.\n- Keep an event-flow breadcrumb for debugging without duplicating item\ncontent.\n- Leave rollout persistence and tool-call telemetry unchanged.\n\nThe item-type match is exhaustive so new response item variants must\nchoose an explicit log label.\n\nRelated to #28224.","tree":{"sha":"4b9bfa308e264dd19a44097b5b8e230282505ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4b9bfa308e264dd19a44097b5b8e230282505ada"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6OGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/C0QAIxuNYo3mkjAPtexYB1n/uJl\nkY/z+p5YA1mkWzmL42ncqNx06LHDKRK5xyTNr80Pmg75IYbFbGaHnbJSDUO8793Q\n+38JDtAJToiEP9o+rpH9wVYdUFPPykjNtZf+ErqGkbZ/n3BdzTZ/cX7bf20lVMYj\n5G5kOIkaBh/PnrYHW3b8DdYeIq6KKD3vM4gx6AJ1mhroWyFRpWNMiiIHZgMKCFSm\nw/mPjLBK9u3iu0ekc1Pvz7NDP4HSagJWov1G+4WozGUb0gdyIBYTyQJ0LucMCqSb\n//bizmURcl7HEuFTe/b81dZIvZ6QnQ+CtAn3iPri8HNSRXs5g6f1vjtrs4xyPkxc\nW6ascawQ3e2YxzMkA+uw0YPXPkCLkyiwKCu+MGAIEdLmEMkc92z0erDltIxMFrqL\n+kCiLcpv8zUFH2Z5fdAEkJl8wCBMvbqevggkBz47AAT8iB+LKSr+JvM+DNzFCV+C\nN3vxTK7VUDXYGjwIKLZg8zbANNRZ7fQq41dtMeeeamfTJn44RdjBIkBXsakZ2j7r\nPq2utRG89T72I66H1YcAJCMQMdY6L/Pd/S4F5d0jUnYGWTvLlRDAbARxXnrnX2EL\nlEamC1kYrVU/oLVTi5h7AiA9eu5FB/SxQwXpVCpZ/zUD7OuWBqEn5QmXQk6r/9PG\nfKmOO0d1t+vcPqoxETjF\n=Llzh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4b9bfa308e264dd19a44097b5b8e230282505ada\nparent acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783604102 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604102 +0100\n\nSummarize streamed response item logs (#31792)\n\n## Why\n\n`handle_non_tool_response_item` logged the complete decoded\n`ResponseItem` at DEBUG. Those values can contain assistant text,\nreasoning content, and tool payloads that are already stored in the\ndurable rollout, making the SQLite copy both redundant and potentially\nlarge or sensitive.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the complete item dump with bounded `item_type` and `item_id`\nfields.\n- Keep an event-flow breadcrumb for debugging without duplicating item\ncontent.\n- Leave rollout persistence and tool-call telemetry unchanged.\n\nThe item-type match is exhaustive so new response item variants must\nchoose an explicit log label.\n\nRelated to #28224.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T13:35:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/538f29ed5da0d1611417148769a1799172bb830e/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43"}]},{"sha":"acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFjYjc4YTQxYTBmMDFiZjY3MWI3N2ZmOGMwNTRmNTAzNDI0YTRjNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:34:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T13:34:47Z"},"message":"Stop persisting RMCP service traces (#31789)\n\n## Why\n\nThe SQLite feedback log enables TRACE by default. `rmcp::service`\nrenders complete MCP service events at TRACE, including large tool\ncatalogs and other protocol payloads. In a busy local sample, this was\nthe largest retained source and individual rows reached about 2 MiB.\n\nThese rows can quickly consume the per-thread retention budget, displace\nsmaller diagnostics, and add unnecessary SQLite insert-and-prune work.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persist `rmcp::service` at INFO and above in the SQLite feedback log.\n- Keep service initialization, shutdown, warnings, and errors available\nfor feedback.\n- Leave other tracing and OpenTelemetry subscribers unchanged.\n\nThis is intentionally target-specific. Broader persistent-log policy\nchanges can remain separate.\n\nRelated to #28224.","tree":{"sha":"2a665765cd032b83e184e31b1cb5ede3561f2e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2a665765cd032b83e184e31b1cb5ede3561f2e89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT6N3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA+YQAHbnCaWzKFoaPz8e4ua2yo85\ncj5I5EDdJ9Gi9MRxEbydALcMze6TnuZujtLX2SbEOSqHRfmcAYcLsYEqWgUuEtzk\ndsqpMTLHgTL3DjaagtbVWCB7ClevoXoodj8HKKw2U9wCm7kNdJ/cJrQA430JCMuE\nNlHBKBstah2dMsBTXEtFDejA6s/kWlT0PiorEeRtYrFTaRrg3gtnZ6Yai15MNi9e\nzD8O+aHmsK/j3GvDAC6OZZzRtvP8jb3EktLtfFBFfkPkHZZROVVXXNG/A6IUU48Z\nzI5u243jgOmdlt1lvJZfblyxW2XEdTKUIZPQp1OT8VrFxIcjoxE2sk7SpiSIyNBG\no0N5l049KWwpHj6+QR/Ss8Lbdtx/27qmMgdsMpN919qrFh4Sd4dfSY5vS63iG+/G\netRf2oI9FNwe+kSJA8OolN6UtjS1HF9dCtcMtCFbwNTJ5R8zYN33gX3cGW4u3diL\n76s/960diTck0m6eIrdZiiLJpvHX5N2nye4La9TasTkaimkNUKyVDRFh4+2fxR6/\ntyX76DsyI+lrsx9+CSVZqefMMpj9xuH28JUwAZnmgJtPwrvLtJPKf5u9KfMs2CTo\nJsaR9swgN2ZI6WFkj1V+a+uAAlV3KrthKPBNmKqdK7inY39vE+VNnl9m5Y6RSWAG\nx01NUV/LfKJlzigGZ5g7\n=P2Ae\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2a665765cd032b83e184e31b1cb5ede3561f2e89\nparent 13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783604087 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783604087 +0100\n\nStop persisting RMCP service traces (#31789)\n\n## Why\n\nThe SQLite feedback log enables TRACE by default. `rmcp::service`\nrenders complete MCP service events at TRACE, including large tool\ncatalogs and other protocol payloads. In a busy local sample, this was\nthe largest retained source and individual rows reached about 2 MiB.\n\nThese rows can quickly consume the per-thread retention budget, displace\nsmaller diagnostics, and add unnecessary SQLite insert-and-prune work.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persist `rmcp::service` at INFO and above in the SQLite feedback log.\n- Keep service initialization, shutdown, warnings, and errors available\nfor feedback.\n- Leave other tracing and OpenTelemetry subscribers unchanged.\n\nThis is intentionally target-specific. Broader persistent-log policy\nchanges can remain separate.\n\nRelated to #28224.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T13:34:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/acb78a41a0f01bf671b77ff8c054f503424a4c43/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781"}]},{"sha":"13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEzYmE4MDU4ZjI5NDcyM2M0N2RiYTVjNDdjYTU4Y2YwOTBmMDQ3ODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T10:17:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T10:17:05Z"},"message":"Resolve selected capability roots without starting executors (#31581)\n\n## Why\n\nA thread can select skill roots that live in an executor environment.\n`skills/list` needs a passive snapshot of the roots that are usable now:\nit must not start an executor, wait for recovery, or reconnect a failed\nenvironment.\n\nThe initial implementation checked the immutable first startup result.\nAfter a successful connection later entered recovery or failed, that\nresult still looked successful. A read-only catalog request could then\nwait for recovery or trigger a new connection while reading the\nfilesystem.\n\n## What\n\n- inspect readiness from the current exec-server connection state\n- return roots only while their environment can serve a request\nimmediately\n- omit environments that have not started, are connecting, or are\nrecovering\n- return warnings for missing environments and terminal connection\nfailures\n- add a fail-fast filesystem view that never starts, waits for, or\nreconnects an environment\n- expose the passive selected-root snapshot through `CodexThread`\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Local and currently connected environments are ready.\n- Starting and recovering environments are omitted without a warning so\ncallers can retry later.\n- Missing and terminally failed environments are omitted with a warning.\n- A disconnect between readiness inspection and filesystem access fails\npromptly instead of crossing into the normal recovery path.\n- Normal model-turn and execution paths keep their existing reconnect\nbehavior.\n\n## Design\n\nThe recovery policy is private to the exec-server client. Callers choose\nthe explicit fail-fast filesystem method; the existing client and\nfilesystem APIs remain reconnecting. This keeps the passive contract at\nthe transport boundary instead of plumbing timeout or retry flags\nthrough the skills stack.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- a lazy stdio environment stays unstarted during passive inspection\n- missing and terminally failed environments surface warnings\n- a real websocket disconnect proves current readiness drops, a\npreviously acquired fail-fast filesystem handle returns promptly, and\nreadiness returns after recovery\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR only provides passive readiness and fail-fast filesystem\nprimitives. It does not add app-server API fields or notifications.\n\n## Stack\n\n- #31582 uses these primitives for experimental thread-scoped\n`skills/list`.\n- #30228 adds targeted invalidation notifications.","tree":{"sha":"7ce1a490888dfa577e696b37fd9ac4f7d551e649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7ce1a490888dfa577e696b37fd9ac4f7d551e649"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT3UhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwC4QADSAqxa/xjnxdp548cmrDkxK\nK8H5McOnEnOHjwhtMy8ph55ZZ+bDC1gQUroenFOKjEGDv629MH99iKwdYB6Sm47Y\n2cUFIXFmjBUgphSb7Isg4gJuToQsRKbtmftzB+dDVCfR/+Sthibt0hfQt9xtWO6D\nOYJs5IVZofNB0Gyp/2AjhLLm2+o27nbORd2kvLJ4Q5SoC+QmS9pPwlDHOHjLMzwr\nYJF+mpK/2uM42rwxRU2AyBURl5jnHCHH+sWziftY2oEzThOvONsYqTntrw8a41yg\nUxPiDqox97JXFUaVKwzO0s17cVz2UozAHwKaOaTY9P6Z35Hlc2I+rO5h4NwO/tty\nUeOgbxwane3A/kC+f/SI2iVE1Kfweppqx1r4Pba0UvJ2BJH837HP4wtpSbN4/20r\nGCMfRdH+eKgMPAdIMVQb1i2v9HGmtTgldPDUiAzdsRkt510+PkezmkOZDB/oN8Oa\nOMkN/Joi+DFiOuIHyTokZO7iONfEjeq2s6ZiIRDpl3ZfjyjTsk8/r1Io+tFHYyGm\np46pZD4BYMUZl+4yH/LpQnFq+398cdfLoXgRyg/Lr5m0ZYmVR9haDMCEHfydhOZr\nWkVQQQPf1LF60i8ZBUME+aTX+GXz6fM37gkCa0i4Zh0tIUwC+dt52AAE0mcgHSJx\nKkGAZNWx5YHvOhhZ2xh8\n=S/V+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ce1a490888dfa577e696b37fd9ac4f7d551e649\nparent 0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783592225 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783592225 +0100\n\nResolve selected capability roots without starting executors (#31581)\n\n## Why\n\nA thread can select skill roots that live in an executor environment.\n`skills/list` needs a passive snapshot of the roots that are usable now:\nit must not start an executor, wait for recovery, or reconnect a failed\nenvironment.\n\nThe initial implementation checked the immutable first startup result.\nAfter a successful connection later entered recovery or failed, that\nresult still looked successful. A read-only catalog request could then\nwait for recovery or trigger a new connection while reading the\nfilesystem.\n\n## What\n\n- inspect readiness from the current exec-server connection state\n- return roots only while their environment can serve a request\nimmediately\n- omit environments that have not started, are connecting, or are\nrecovering\n- return warnings for missing environments and terminal connection\nfailures\n- add a fail-fast filesystem view that never starts, waits for, or\nreconnects an environment\n- expose the passive selected-root snapshot through `CodexThread`\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Local and currently connected environments are ready.\n- Starting and recovering environments are omitted without a warning so\ncallers can retry later.\n- Missing and terminally failed environments are omitted with a warning.\n- A disconnect between readiness inspection and filesystem access fails\npromptly instead of crossing into the normal recovery path.\n- Normal model-turn and execution paths keep their existing reconnect\nbehavior.\n\n## Design\n\nThe recovery policy is private to the exec-server client. Callers choose\nthe explicit fail-fast filesystem method; the existing client and\nfilesystem APIs remain reconnecting. This keeps the passive contract at\nthe transport boundary instead of plumbing timeout or retry flags\nthrough the skills stack.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- a lazy stdio environment stays unstarted during passive inspection\n- missing and terminally failed environments surface warnings\n- a real websocket disconnect proves current readiness drops, a\npreviously acquired fail-fast filesystem handle returns promptly, and\nreadiness returns after recovery\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR only provides passive readiness and fail-fast filesystem\nprimitives. It does not add app-server API fields or notifications.\n\n## Stack\n\n- #31582 uses these primitives for experimental thread-scoped\n`skills/list`.\n- #30228 adds targeted invalidation notifications.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T10:17:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13ba8058f294723c47dba5c47ca58cf090f04781/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688"}]},{"sha":"0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBkMThkNGY3NTM1ZDkzY2U3ZmQwZmZhOWNhNjk5MzczMjEzNTI2ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T09:12:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T09:12:30Z"},"message":"test(skills): assert symlinked metadata loading (#31756)\n\n## Why\n\nThe host walk-inventory test writes policy metadata for a symlinked\nskill, but only asserted the loaded names. It could still pass if\nmetadata loading regressed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Compare the complete loaded skill metadata.\n- Verify the first skill keeps `allow_implicit_invocation: false` while\nthe sibling has no policy.\n\nStacked on #31566.","tree":{"sha":"354842359d3f6228ef5d58df3fe0e29feba14421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/354842359d3f6228ef5d58df3fe0e29feba14421"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT2X+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAghAQADsXbtWLlCX8r2/XkopJ9RLn\n0ruY2XovfI9A9tY9tThT8gihJ0Wi0fSZBrf8m610MJIC1EELmmgaDOzaTqQXleku\nl1Y/7gIO2JfD1ZtegpG97t1msA05d8yX8I8v5k7fixdWb+HZIQ435CYilbjTpUit\nI3Yo6jVlDgsOjW9wtH3J4+kxYCh7lReJYFh38vURcmwIbOyrvoL5IUwYFXp1lyTx\nKgTbPwxwcIWp+e/WjbWee4MpPHSKb7kvHxGN669bZUh6VP3pWunPFHA7UGxjF3Ee\nvdCDHpM8tRqkCTM6J3PiJQVWA1VbJU3MvS3enBM3hUXocmljE5iHc6yaMj4goFga\nbZ2ixCrcNHoyWXk+pfpYWofjr7C/pCwYbMROnLLYtZhoArQ4cq71ZoYZi+lEzOni\nchE+HBZMNe3vJDCtCFjKBUNO6jmKvL5zfKRL1VC3OMlADmhaXiVQBwZXyoJm+w1X\nakxR+N4of86iXAseC/GYSw6rkoGqdQbpYZLz/Wb5c81NRYvV7l5sdCup68TQaWbS\ndusb9P307cEPexiYQNMrBH4tQko+5eI5d6qo+CXgUqmqBpgry81mMki+f4TyaJMT\nsPj9sFxDQxiWyg2QAX6++7xQAeBhXk0OyQ7s9rLNAVPGUCLh90nAfCXXdEza7s4E\n8dkLbTgv0Tw8HOtEn6qo\n=lnog\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 354842359d3f6228ef5d58df3fe0e29feba14421\nparent e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783588350 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783588350 +0100\n\ntest(skills): assert symlinked metadata loading (#31756)\n\n## Why\n\nThe host walk-inventory test writes policy metadata for a symlinked\nskill, but only asserted the loaded names. It could still pass if\nmetadata loading regressed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Compare the complete loaded skill metadata.\n- Verify the first skill keeps `allow_implicit_invocation: false` while\nthe sibling has no policy.\n\nStacked on #31566.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T09:12:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0d18d4f7535d93ce7fd0ffa9ca69937321352688/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400"}]},{"sha":"e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUzOThhOTllZGY5MWQ5MzQ1NGU3MzY2MjMzYjE3ODkzNzYzMTE0MDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:56:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:56:14Z"},"message":"Bound exec-server process event reordering (#31576)\n\n## Why\n\nA malicious exec-server can send out-of-order process notifications\nfaster than missing events arrive. The client retained every future\nevent in a per-session reorder map, so many tiny events or a few large\noutput chunks could grow orchestrator memory without bound.\n\n## What changed\n\n- cap each session's pending process-event reorder state at 256 events\nand 1 MiB\n- reject individual process events larger than 1 MiB\n- release byte accounting as events publish or a session fails\n- fail and detach only the affected process session when a limit is\nexceeded\n- let the next expected event drain a full buffer, so the limits apply\nto retained future state\n- apply the same bounded insertion path during reconnect recovery while\nsafely handling dense tail output, missing exit events, newer live\nnotifications, and conflicting `Closed` sequences\n\nSequence distance is intentionally not capped because it does not affect\nallocation; the event-count and byte limits are the resource-exhaustion\nboundary.\n\n## Tests\n\nFocused exec-server tests cover oversized output, full count/byte\nbuffers, gap-closing delivery, dense recovery interleaved with newer\nnotifications, missing exit reconstruction, and conflicting terminal\nsequences.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is limited to per-session process-event reorder state. It does not\nintroduce a scheduler, quota framework, or new public configuration.","tree":{"sha":"8eb9b55145b5facb334b1c38da11b36d5455f509","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8eb9b55145b5facb334b1c38da11b36d5455f509"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT2IuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMHMQAC8Ex21KW0DXnfbzzlnSUY5E\nIqTcyDNeN4CgY5FuD38i/dON74jKdNRbXMDSwD7zadMFPf71GhZ9MRCNSqCfGO/o\nqEenSeMKK6oENG5QrhMa66ScoSMV+I3vX90hUumhLsUtCXuRLpGDI2pPYc72GOWR\nKoIBPKeRKH1ooKYwnPz5N9hBvaFf5d7+h0v0YZzLtcfxjAFBVuCT1bfsm4NUxms7\nJvgfVCvThOFauzsymsHGWZGcH+Cmn1rp8kccMYyszM5uQNRESanI/EZDAw6K/p74\niG0nmW+9jyqwjdK059P4snEbr4Q8EKYxSWIVNjePTOnj0HeuYkBx7H4wGIca3N8q\nfZtnelW9dQpT4XkCNc+DjSYKEH+FOSRBAIdxdNbKJdhB78okqhsXquWkTB/WZKbp\n48xifWKEECl6+UDmYIU7hvfC8oUThJDoJI4d7FOQOMjjnnFdGNyh8W5hL3biYSCO\ncuBFzN/RTjcIiTNVK5OTwnebXMfyGeY98mlqcELcDfc4k/dYZnfEhh6ZSioDU3n6\nIbovObgxnG0KzZ2hOSF/wHR8nP2ws12MxaStOE4h27bupMEiHiKTSrclF+8RB2cy\nOTtDjGFb/Ggq54RCaI5pIF33ChvqQvHUhir6IGrMO8rpW/E0REsFURzp1WYzD5PB\nZm3cgSuuhjlctmdipqyq\n=sL5H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8eb9b55145b5facb334b1c38da11b36d5455f509\nparent e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783587374 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783587374 +0100\n\nBound exec-server process event reordering (#31576)\n\n## Why\n\nA malicious exec-server can send out-of-order process notifications\nfaster than missing events arrive. The client retained every future\nevent in a per-session reorder map, so many tiny events or a few large\noutput chunks could grow orchestrator memory without bound.\n\n## What changed\n\n- cap each session's pending process-event reorder state at 256 events\nand 1 MiB\n- reject individual process events larger than 1 MiB\n- release byte accounting as events publish or a session fails\n- fail and detach only the affected process session when a limit is\nexceeded\n- let the next expected event drain a full buffer, so the limits apply\nto retained future state\n- apply the same bounded insertion path during reconnect recovery while\nsafely handling dense tail output, missing exit events, newer live\nnotifications, and conflicting `Closed` sequences\n\nSequence distance is intentionally not capped because it does not affect\nallocation; the event-count and byte limits are the resource-exhaustion\nboundary.\n\n## Tests\n\nFocused exec-server tests cover oversized output, full count/byte\nbuffers, gap-closing delivery, dense recovery interleaved with newer\nnotifications, missing exit reconstruction, and conflicting terminal\nsequences.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is limited to per-session process-event reorder state. It does not\nintroduce a scheduler, quota framework, or new public configuration.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T08:56:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e398a99edf91d93454e7366233b1789376311400/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e"}]},{"sha":"e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU4ZWI2MDA5MmE5NWZlODdiZmE1MmJjMjYxYjJjYjg1NzMxZTQyN2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:54:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:54:24Z"},"message":"perf(skills): reuse walk inventory for host loading (#31566)\n\n## Why\n\nCCA thread startup loads repository skills through the primary remote\nenvironment. This still used the older host skill loader, which\nrecursively issued directory and metadata requests over the exec-server\nconnection. On a high-latency connection, one skill scan could turn into\nhundreds of round trips.\n\nExecutor-selected skill roots already avoid this pattern: they use one\nbounded filesystem walk, reuse the returned inventory, and overlap\nindependent reads.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extract the URI-native walk inventory into a shared private discovery\nmodule.\n- Use that discovery path for both environment-owned and host/repository\nskill roots.\n- Reuse the walk inventory to avoid per-skill metadata existence checks\nwhen the inventory is complete.\n- Canonicalize host skill identities and parse skill files with bounded\nconcurrency.\n- Prune hidden host directories during traversal, preserving visible\naliases and walk limits.\n- Cache namespace probes by ancestor and keep all remote namespace reads\nunder the same concurrency bound.\n- Keep safe metadata probes for incomplete walks, file symlinks, and\ncase aliases.\n\n## Dependency\n\n#31570 is now merged. It provides the optional `pruneHiddenDirectories`\nwalk flag used here. That flag defaults to false and is omitted when\ndisabled.\n\nNo other exec-server API changes are introduced.","tree":{"sha":"4233a3ea5e99dcebd28f3eb219f5459c195a4374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4233a3ea5e99dcebd28f3eb219f5459c195a4374"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT2HACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMQgQAH/D+IYwCA9+m9eoaiBvaqIL\nvKOSKJunj/9Dgv/Uwm0G6zdeko4hhkV5JFsaVLB0NUqmeymVQzgOIUZgSd4rUIXp\njIb5aF5HJAOIQ8i6NlWAz+m8gHgLv/XxZjgjwlgRQgBpQvWCFAhid/CWZCAXr4fs\nlerf+SpCULrS3a5RCMuRmAvlWKwQAXArn6iGz/u+LbIcculQYx3Ha0xd2E+LTAi3\nBuvKZQi6R7n8gYfvrb8sbQ9TiXX8SLFJ32lzSwXF+y+BiH2UL8LVos1759T4wuqp\nfiwPUMt6nIaEr12jKQgbT7LVsmfXtg/HbI/UNHLxOMNtDEiLOLYeKxgGGhgejOuM\nO76xwOraiyUD3Wsr3s7ppGACD1+IUxAybv+abjYRywP+8PR3Xrp4uqjDewlIXazl\n0mt2VMZnxLwD2UVFcHPk2TpAkECmqiMGFNGYw9M5vTZv3gFCyP8F79HBBN9oiwbL\n0uGIa3qAeLoOs+ZoxfsGTwMXYHdZmu+bMvq39BxfF+g7R0fT8u9bP5mJxB7dalLq\npjlXJ74+8U8EXC3Z3EuUnCTnrq7nxnABXW+tooWGX+hI4UPV5fYHf6Brp3kOjyat\nvYxMR/icZrnMBwNNDncUnRrPB3D4Ym05VRGzUwkV4mJAJWLFQmGakxDc2agmLwR4\npwwgJo/A6sLzLkL4Y0CM\n=tzbc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4233a3ea5e99dcebd28f3eb219f5459c195a4374\nparent 89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1783587264 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783587264 +0100\n\nperf(skills): reuse walk inventory for host loading (#31566)\n\n## Why\n\nCCA thread startup loads repository skills through the primary remote\nenvironment. This still used the older host skill loader, which\nrecursively issued directory and metadata requests over the exec-server\nconnection. On a high-latency connection, one skill scan could turn into\nhundreds of round trips.\n\nExecutor-selected skill roots already avoid this pattern: they use one\nbounded filesystem walk, reuse the returned inventory, and overlap\nindependent reads.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extract the URI-native walk inventory into a shared private discovery\nmodule.\n- Use that discovery path for both environment-owned and host/repository\nskill roots.\n- Reuse the walk inventory to avoid per-skill metadata existence checks\nwhen the inventory is complete.\n- Canonicalize host skill identities and parse skill files with bounded\nconcurrency.\n- Prune hidden host directories during traversal, preserving visible\naliases and walk limits.\n- Cache namespace probes by ancestor and keep all remote namespace reads\nunder the same concurrency bound.\n- Keep safe metadata probes for incomplete walks, file symlinks, and\ncase aliases.\n\n## Dependency\n\n#31570 is now merged. It provides the optional `pruneHiddenDirectories`\nwalk flag used here. That flag defaults to false and is omitted when\ndisabled.\n\nNo other exec-server API changes are introduced.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T08:54:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e8eb60092a95fe87bfa52bc261b2cb85731e427e/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74"}]},{"sha":"89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg5YWVhZTZjMjFiMWM2MjY4MDAyZGUzNTgwYzg4M2MyYmE4MDBlNzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:50:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T08:50:11Z"},"message":"core: route realtime and memories through HTTP client factory (#31362)\n\n## Why\n\n`ModelClient` already carries the `HttpClientFactory` resolved from\nsession configuration, but realtime call creation and memory\nsummarization still constructed the legacy default client directly.\nConsequently, those first-party API requests could ignore\n`features.respect_system_proxy` even when Responses traffic honored it.\n\nThese are the final direct default-client constructions in\n`core/src/client.rs`, so they form one small migration unit on top of\n#31361.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generalize `build_responses_transport` to `build_api_transport`.\n- Route realtime call creation through the helper using the selected\nprovider and `/realtime/calls` destination.\n- Route `/memories/trace_summarize` through the same helper.\n- Remove the now-unused direct `build_reqwest_client` import.\n\n## Review guide\n\n1. The helper rename at the bottom of `core/src/client.rs` is mechanical\nand keeps existing Responses behavior unchanged.\n2. The realtime call path computes the route from the final provider,\nincluding `api_provider_override`.\n3. The memories path supplies its existing endpoint to the same API\nroute class.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\n## Follow-up\n\nDirect HTTP clients outside `ModelClient` remain separate migration\nslices.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31362).\n* #31637\n* #31431\n* #31363\n* __->__ #31362","tree":{"sha":"ba48d989670f93911169b7737527767ce7905ce5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ba48d989670f93911169b7737527767ce7905ce5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT2DDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfNYQAADFaDZvpLPr8MMoGa75qB+E\nnDZcHNMjE+UQ50AxOd21H8II2NB7qSEKtF1s+XfhQdPM01JwWhDnO++f6Z3WiXZ2\nXD6vMJVXU1kXs2t2sz5Fotr6YG0Ola9T4x0oPh30zoq2ec4JkpT2gWHumyp8978M\nH/u52oKD9WljJBuIW0s4l1+bf5I1xoqpAYhUh59IQdDkeLxgqL9gxyl1fxV+mzJ6\nWQ+aM90DDL6Gxm1ChQVJWC/0gIKp+nd8HV+bhEwnjSsdFqU9sB5HtY1UIoIL6of4\nBDEc/+/jot3tEsUBBYYYTiDxcMWsTo3I3NIY1UXXDx7k+Rar6jfkwCIka7QrmCUD\nsIafNAbc2GEZ0fLLRI9GhmDxUanNMbK1QyvqoQHdWQ9CZ9Yg4W8unOMjt5+NEEuM\nfVDloeDcT2kJpuqx5TR1xRn63Q10ohC09md/uE8PDaaVgtZGShy7RiplNbbZDJKW\nmdt5zviRjFar7smpBQnfYUA8Nui82oJmt7GQbqReGwxAxvc1UBb7BIWiWx0Fm0v3\nMa8sbR4E8u4L/lmqlOaluIIPQwdFmj5AR6uv+2hqw0KgcmppzUUjjnr56uiKGguo\nypr2uDILZNQVJflUVHzKnsV2Qw+Vm5q9HuKlzASI4Xzo62kz4M4/DeAdZeR5vWjq\nR8fJAxMt3sHxVUgjZrM/\n=K4H1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ba48d989670f93911169b7737527767ce7905ce5\nparent dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1783587011 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783587011 -0700\n\ncore: route realtime and memories through HTTP client factory (#31362)\n\n## Why\n\n`ModelClient` already carries the `HttpClientFactory` resolved from\nsession configuration, but realtime call creation and memory\nsummarization still constructed the legacy default client directly.\nConsequently, those first-party API requests could ignore\n`features.respect_system_proxy` even when Responses traffic honored it.\n\nThese are the final direct default-client constructions in\n`core/src/client.rs`, so they form one small migration unit on top of\n#31361.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generalize `build_responses_transport` to `build_api_transport`.\n- Route realtime call creation through the helper using the selected\nprovider and `/realtime/calls` destination.\n- Route `/memories/trace_summarize` through the same helper.\n- Remove the now-unused direct `build_reqwest_client` import.\n\n## Review guide\n\n1. The helper rename at the bottom of `core/src/client.rs` is mechanical\nand keeps existing Responses behavior unchanged.\n2. The realtime call path computes the route from the final provider,\nincluding `api_provider_override`.\n3. The memories path supplies its existing endpoint to the same API\nroute class.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check --tests -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\n## Follow-up\n\nDirect HTTP clients outside `ModelClient` remain separate migration\nslices.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/31362).\n* #31637\n* #31431\n* #31363\n* __->__ #31362","verified_at":"2026-07-09T08:50:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89aeae6c21b1c6268002de3580c883c2ba800e74/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f"}]},{"sha":"dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRjMjNjN2JjYzhmZDU0M2ZlNzI3YzdiNDQ0N2EzZDc4NTgzNjkzMmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"efrazer-oai","email":"efrazer@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T05:08:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T05:08:00Z"},"message":"fix: parse compact release metadata in installer (#31667)\n\n# Summary\n\nGitHub's latest-release endpoint can return compact, single-line JSON.\nThe standalone installer treated release metadata as line-oriented text,\nso those responses could make asset lookup fail even though the\nrequested assets were present.\n\nThe regression was introduced by\n[#31056](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31056). That change reused\nthe `/releases/latest` metadata response for both version resolution and\nasset lookup, exposing the existing formatting-sensitive asset parser to\ncompact responses from that endpoint.\n\nThis change parses the release metadata once with a one-pass POSIX awk\nscanner. The scanner tracks JSON strings and nesting, extracts the root\nrelease tag plus direct asset name/digest pairs, and produces the same\nresult regardless of whitespace or object field order. It uses POSIX\n`fold` to bound awk record sizes so compact responses stay fast across\nawk implementations.\n\nFixes #31520.\n\n## Changes\n\n- replace line-oriented release metadata matching with structure-aware\nparsing\n- reuse the parsed metadata for latest-version and asset-digest lookup\n- add regression coverage for compact JSON, reordered fields, nested\ndecoys, and JSON-looking release text\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Keep the installer dependency-free by using standard POSIX tools\nalready required by the shell installer.\n- Parse only the GitHub release fields the installer consumes, in one\npass, instead of vendoring a general JSON library.\n- Preserve asset-object boundaries so nested or string-encoded `name`\nand `digest` fields cannot be mistaken for release assets.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Tests: focused installer suite locally and on Linux.\n- Smoke tests: real pretty and compact GitHub release metadata,\nlatest-release resolution, and checksum-asset selection.\n- Portability: macOS awk plus Linux gawk, mawk, and nawk.\n- Stress coverage: randomized formatting and field order, adversarial\nnested/string content, and a synthetic 2,000-asset compact response.","tree":{"sha":"805612c35f10f2f4262c1b8b954025a257357198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/805612c35f10f2f4262c1b8b954025a257357198"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTyywCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhUUQADOzn+3O4xWdm+kliZJzs27b\n+3G4I/1kEk1C/S9mo1K9Nz015bJw0vaWJAvRbhFhZea/DYGP0G9ZQgdC1e9gY+Li\ne6bDLwIiRjNcmyZTKX2fIboVZxUjs//vkG1cEsuSrWr4LYHpSfQ5BWQaZbnWc69i\nZmBCnzUFMSJd9LXb8SBVC/kkOP7pIMpwdu7y8CwzTc7Bdm46uNzAQdie4Q/HHH8A\n6ZFYrhwIfH/HzD1xMWv4HXW4+yXJyhY9Rb/Jn/QHNL3eo1nmh0ZQIvp4xqae2YgG\npXqvfj0thqvmUxLQLbbx2WCgGRea7PN8P0mWHjDeG5N2uhXfYjnnVqs+vWW7jrIT\nhm1NUh2XhpI4o92dkpJAliObq6LNJwupU7Tbjnp6MGnKRP0J3Lgfu1ZVNYBbikhG\ngCL15GdizBsFeXOrRMVn0NHLgqzH51r002J6yzBqgPgVGMJv6ZuNBm8JZDWyJlTI\niBAB5NAt8KiKVJYA1BthK6y5n9vQk/JzqdTpXU9j44ZPR+st6pd2d0cD1b29fd8e\nxH3fFrfcjQ7W8OueqTeAAyuxJrcuaFkd+a1/xI0M+Ldh8LKxTBDClEp1vAF69AcM\nPPWBdtV1jiaJRLKwGMfrQq2SF1qvbppUHrdhQr5ffmPVlIN4SIBgXSMPt1zWLa5/\nRNRMo+R/ZsmgWDsmBrts\n=9NEY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 805612c35f10f2f4262c1b8b954025a257357198\nparent 3380969a29134630d56feb6218e8e8dcc5e8196d\nauthor efrazer-oai <efrazer@openai.com> 1783573680 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783573680 -0700\n\nfix: parse compact release metadata in installer (#31667)\n\n# Summary\n\nGitHub's latest-release endpoint can return compact, single-line JSON.\nThe standalone installer treated release metadata as line-oriented text,\nso those responses could make asset lookup fail even though the\nrequested assets were present.\n\nThe regression was introduced by\n[#31056](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31056). That change reused\nthe `/releases/latest` metadata response for both version resolution and\nasset lookup, exposing the existing formatting-sensitive asset parser to\ncompact responses from that endpoint.\n\nThis change parses the release metadata once with a one-pass POSIX awk\nscanner. The scanner tracks JSON strings and nesting, extracts the root\nrelease tag plus direct asset name/digest pairs, and produces the same\nresult regardless of whitespace or object field order. It uses POSIX\n`fold` to bound awk record sizes so compact responses stay fast across\nawk implementations.\n\nFixes #31520.\n\n## Changes\n\n- replace line-oriented release metadata matching with structure-aware\nparsing\n- reuse the parsed metadata for latest-version and asset-digest lookup\n- add regression coverage for compact JSON, reordered fields, nested\ndecoys, and JSON-looking release text\n\n## Design decisions\n\n- Keep the installer dependency-free by using standard POSIX tools\nalready required by the shell installer.\n- Parse only the GitHub release fields the installer consumes, in one\npass, instead of vendoring a general JSON library.\n- Preserve asset-object boundaries so nested or string-encoded `name`\nand `digest` fields cannot be mistaken for release assets.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Tests: focused installer suite locally and on Linux.\n- Smoke tests: real pretty and compact GitHub release metadata,\nlatest-release resolution, and checksum-asset selection.\n- Portability: macOS awk plus Linux gawk, mawk, and nawk.\n- Stress coverage: randomized formatting and field order, adversarial\nnested/string content, and a synthetic 2,000-asset compact response.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T05:08:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dc23c7bcc8fd543fe727c7b4447a3d785836932f/comments","author":{"login":"efrazer-oai","id":263771262,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7jUfg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263771262?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/efrazer-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/efrazer-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gi