ent factory (#31361)","verified_at":"2026-07-09T02:32:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5892c7b69dc0ce551f061a9baa52b875bb9e4f72","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5892c7b69dc0ce551f061a9baa52b875bb9e4f72","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5892c7b69dc0ce551f061a9baa52b875bb9e4f72/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907"}]},{"sha":"555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1NWFhNzlkNWFiNGMwMTExOTZhMWY5ZmQwOGM2ZTY2NzNkZDA5MDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"stevenlee-oai","email":"stevenlee@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:46:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:46:11Z"},"message":"[connectors] Refresh codex_apps /ps/mcp auth (#31486)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019f2408-dc59-79f2-b245-4c11debd1a61](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019f2408-dc59-79f2-b245-4c11debd1a61)\n\n## Why\n\nLong-lived Codex sessions can outlive the ChatGPT bearer token that was\npresent when the MCP runtime started.\n\nThe Responses path already recovers from token expiration by refreshing\nor reloading the shared `AuthManager`. The reserved `codex_apps`\nhosted-plugin client did not observe that update: `McpConnectionManager`\nbuilt its `/ps/mcp` HTTP auth once from a `CodexAuth` snapshot, and\n`auth_provider_from_auth` copied that snapshot bearer into a static\n`BearerAuthProvider`.\n\nAfter the copied bearer expired, `/ps/mcp` kept sending it even though\nResponses had a newer token in the same `AuthManager`. The failure\noccurred before downstream connector execution, so unrelated apps such\nas Gmail, Slack, and Google Calendar could all fail with the same\ntransport-level `401 token_expired`.\n\nThis replaces\n[openai/codex#29474](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29474), which\nwas closed for inactivity without being merged. A new long-lived-session\nreport reproduced the same simultaneous `/ps/mcp` expiry pattern across\nunrelated apps.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add an `AuthManager`-backed request-header provider in\n`codex-model-provider`. It keeps an `Arc<AuthManager>` and reads\n`auth_cached()` for each outbound request, so the next `/ps/mcp` call\nsees a token refreshed by the existing Responses/auth-recovery flow.\n- Scope that provider to the startup account, ChatGPT user, and\nworkspace identity. Same-identity token reloads are followed; an account\nswitch emits no ambient auth until account-scoped MCP state is rebuilt.\n- Have `McpConnectionManager` construct the dynamic provider only for\nthe reserved `codex_apps` registration used by the hosted-plugin\n`/ps/mcp` path.\n\n| MCP path | Auth behavior after this change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Reserved `codex_apps` hosted-plugin `/ps/mcp` | Read current\nsame-identity auth from the shared `AuthManager` per request |\n| `codex_apps` with `CODEX_CONNECTORS_TOKEN` | Keep the environment\nbearer-token override |\n| User-configured/direct MCP registrations | Keep their existing\nconfigured auth path |\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No plugin-service changes.\n- No downstream Slack, Gmail, Calendar, or other connector\nOAuth/link-refresh changes.\n- No auth UI changes.\n- No behavior change for user-configured/direct MCP registrations.\n- No new `/ps/mcp`-initiated token refresh; this makes `/ps/mcp` observe\nrefreshes already performed through the shared `AuthManager`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`\n- Covers same-identity token reloads and refuses a changed startup\nidentity.\n- `just test -p codex-mcp`\n- `just test -p codex-core mcp_auth_refresh`\n- Creates the reserved hosted-plugin `codex_apps` `/ps/mcp` client\nbefore the shared `AuthManager` changes, updates that same manager\nthrough its public external-auth path, performs a real `tools/call`, and\nasserts the request uses the current bearer.","tree":{"sha":"a91345fdc24c1782bca9709943c761b34329e48b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a91345fdc24c1782bca9709943c761b34329e48b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTv1jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmr0QAGa2BhdVgMK3JzXMMC4dAe+6\nCouN8/vWPVguNkgitoXIG5QawD38/4yGUrAj9wKp1O4CevEPjqGfbYI149vQ9mS6\nJ19tgPuE/Yxzu6MCNuYS4ztQyy7kaMmMsPM9YXmYeX1BFe2t1M21UB5ziBsCgNzk\nU2PT08zgVFCVIJwGJPH4ndinnU3kvlMm8hm6zRegIY32xQ9DaZFqYY1J9AARvJxx\n+0HbpxpBXcaSfNUofXM2Hs27kiNHxRCRWh8h1JUyVoZoJTtpNCFMNZdHfl5V795S\n4ei2XllOj99F+WCyvTGEr29CQQ3s0H2YgLGmWyDWTsrD4n3dheibEY0naX34XoEA\n7AGgNGoozfkH3Urp3NI53cph5HGOskn2B26j5gSlrUWazXaH2/Q8lUIkY8aZL6z/\nC4TywVwmnQg/96RzzjQBEpDBl0qEZWBScX7BdBOHOS+XBY67TjRNOYLTfLP4kmju\niE/TqK8+wQAl1ce4VGtvbwJdi6VX89vIh0nDANPGjv73z5a8WV0S82BCN/w/EA3P\neVBG7uLP527oUUerxJ+PnOgUMUoy62mKvvtpbk7iJ9vWmgniTiOeSMvqX0PgLR2F\n615O7EKMDJgxSINbYcmUUYfYTOYCz3tVvnTGlG0eHI2477sS7nPC8sDbZymZyddy\nAL1NIVdqNCw2tOFqjXSV\n=44If\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a91345fdc24c1782bca9709943c761b34329e48b\nparent 20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa\nauthor stevenlee-oai <stevenlee@openai.com> 1783561571 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783561571 -0400\n\n[connectors] Refresh codex_apps /ps/mcp auth (#31486)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019f2408-dc59-79f2-b245-4c11debd1a61](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019f2408-dc59-79f2-b245-4c11debd1a61)\n\n## Why\n\nLong-lived Codex sessions can outlive the ChatGPT bearer token that was\npresent when the MCP runtime started.\n\nThe Responses path already recovers from token expiration by refreshing\nor reloading the shared `AuthManager`. The reserved `codex_apps`\nhosted-plugin client did not observe that update: `McpConnectionManager`\nbuilt its `/ps/mcp` HTTP auth once from a `CodexAuth` snapshot, and\n`auth_provider_from_auth` copied that snapshot bearer into a static\n`BearerAuthProvider`.\n\nAfter the copied bearer expired, `/ps/mcp` kept sending it even though\nResponses had a newer token in the same `AuthManager`. The failure\noccurred before downstream connector execution, so unrelated apps such\nas Gmail, Slack, and Google Calendar could all fail with the same\ntransport-level `401 token_expired`.\n\nThis replaces\n[openai/codex#29474](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29474), which\nwas closed for inactivity without being merged. A new long-lived-session\nreport reproduced the same simultaneous `/ps/mcp` expiry pattern across\nunrelated apps.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add an `AuthManager`-backed request-header provider in\n`codex-model-provider`. It keeps an `Arc<AuthManager>` and reads\n`auth_cached()` for each outbound request, so the next `/ps/mcp` call\nsees a token refreshed by the existing Responses/auth-recovery flow.\n- Scope that provider to the startup account, ChatGPT user, and\nworkspace identity. Same-identity token reloads are followed; an account\nswitch emits no ambient auth until account-scoped MCP state is rebuilt.\n- Have `McpConnectionManager` construct the dynamic provider only for\nthe reserved `codex_apps` registration used by the hosted-plugin\n`/ps/mcp` path.\n\n| MCP path | Auth behavior after this change |\n| --- | --- |\n| Reserved `codex_apps` hosted-plugin `/ps/mcp` | Read current\nsame-identity auth from the shared `AuthManager` per request |\n| `codex_apps` with `CODEX_CONNECTORS_TOKEN` | Keep the environment\nbearer-token override |\n| User-configured/direct MCP registrations | Keep their existing\nconfigured auth path |\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No plugin-service changes.\n- No downstream Slack, Gmail, Calendar, or other connector\nOAuth/link-refresh changes.\n- No auth UI changes.\n- No behavior change for user-configured/direct MCP registrations.\n- No new `/ps/mcp`-initiated token refresh; this makes `/ps/mcp` observe\nrefreshes already performed through the shared `AuthManager`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`\n- Covers same-identity token reloads and refuses a changed startup\nidentity.\n- `just test -p codex-mcp`\n- `just test -p codex-core mcp_auth_refresh`\n- Creates the reserved hosted-plugin `codex_apps` `/ps/mcp` client\nbefore the shared `AuthManager` changes, updates that same manager\nthrough its public external-auth path, performs a real `tools/call`, and\nasserts the request uses the current bearer.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:46:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555aa79d5ab4c011196a1f9fd08c6e6673dd0907/comments","author":{"login":"stevenlee-oai","id":213687449,"node_id":"U_kgDODLycmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213687449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stevenlee-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa"}]},{"sha":"20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIwZTVlZGZhNzRkNDRiMmU3NjdmYTUyYTFkMzc2OWE0ZjY1ZDQ5ZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:04:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T01:04:44Z"},"message":"Expand agent core ownership (#31675)\n\nThe agent core team owns the core agent implementation and should review\nchanges to its adjacent runtime crates. Those crates were not covered by\nthe existing CODEOWNERS rules.\n\nThis adds `@openai/codex-core-agent-team` ownership for:\n\n- `codex-rs/arg0`\n- `codex-rs/codex-mcp`\n- `codex-rs/exec-server`\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNo runtime tests are applicable because this only changes CODEOWNERS\nmetadata.","tree":{"sha":"045d5eaf536063a3deb2b68943d342a8365169b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/045d5eaf536063a3deb2b68943d342a8365169b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvOsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5f4QAHpQSQPROXql27rgngdM+PiQ\nKRvx2/vdx6R2VBCUoI08PybrYffRoFzYP7DYnuyGIeQg4ZkTKZAcsrS0A/PBdZ11\nXuIqJrrW1y2JZzfkF0gMRvQwOdYetMJF+rF1dP+lAmc7djFnVHYiuhvAxvvv+NAl\n4lyfHoKWSlsVtG3l9qT2h/Pzv1xkpKTopw6tzP6TRBTXcNfHTX5R3mPdazN5jein\nXcRNG68r3PKsNLW1APvfmc6bu9mJBCPDxk7jWnMAHuqIKVRMLTyQlhraGo6VW+KV\nHuwi2rbc/BoQJEGsR8SBlxYhCW33TwFhRiixPINLnQR3AGyyIxGBhs+GazRgh6X1\nElgFN+S5mFikNQdjjtquDP3P/K09N7L+V1kTt4yrYFhXp+zz2eFDWAaGx7Wa310Z\nZOE+jKEhRNlOpBvSvcx+Jfy1PtrvldKRWMlKxdp2Ka/THXdPgy2lyVeugADoOhKz\nYmvbvGKRWu50BXKAWRjzNMConD+ngrRmcaDRFvdEbyfAwXxP3fby/ig1r9Gc1JDV\nbEr23JRv1YR5mAu8llJmzq6VDhefj90MAHd7SlMpZGTRLjQXe/ajONLcXE35VYLl\nvCy5LcJJYwU1DFY9ujHpd5cyruUSvN0bxJi3EnHC9tBO+lFL2ylbDqJv/bJKSntX\nw3io7fiE9WWsRCPZV4yf\n=NT5D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 045d5eaf536063a3deb2b68943d342a8365169b3\nparent 0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1783559084 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783559084 -0700\n\nExpand agent core ownership (#31675)\n\nThe agent core team owns the core agent implementation and should review\nchanges to its adjacent runtime crates. Those crates were not covered by\nthe existing CODEOWNERS rules.\n\nThis adds `@openai/codex-core-agent-team` ownership for:\n\n- `codex-rs/arg0`\n- `codex-rs/codex-mcp`\n- `codex-rs/exec-server`\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNo runtime tests are applicable because this only changes CODEOWNERS\nmetadata.","verified_at":"2026-07-09T01:04:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20e5edfa74d44b2e767fa52a1d3769a4f65d49fa/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8"}]},{"sha":"0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA3NDZlOGEzNDU3NGI0YmY0NzIxNjcyYzk3ZmM2YTk0ZmQ4YmZhZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:58:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:58:28Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve reviewer when resuming threads (#30278)\n\n## Why\n\nA thread resumed without an explicit reviewer could pick up the reviewer\nfrom the current config instead of preserving the reviewer already in\nuse by the thread. After an app restart, this meant a thread running\nwith auto review could silently switch back to user review, and the next\nturn could continue under the wrong reviewer.\n\n## What changed\n\nPersist the effective reviewer with each turn and restore the latest\npersisted value when the thread resumes. If the resume request\nexplicitly provides a reviewer, that value still takes precedence.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Added a regression test that starts a thread with auto review, records\na turn, restarts with user review in config, resumes without an\noverride, and verifies that auto review is preserved.\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_preserves_persisted_approvals_reviewer`\n- Clippy for the affected crates","tree":{"sha":"4f1beb9b414ca552aa6624b4394bcee886684a75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4f1beb9b414ca552aa6624b4394bcee886684a75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTvI0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6xoQAIiX9Y5EESqtrr03u5ecQg0U\nE6ktZ22TeMLkg1896X8G8Mk8EZlUpAiLgzoGsF0wKdtW1r8gE683WEwYnoCT1xBn\n/MLD1JoTQiSO/MK7VDCJ6BbDyMpcrAbvvrO/iXQr2sVdwWSv645LkwVNF29ap7t3\nfFQLTF/Rawhnow+KtXRMuVV//clFBDVU9PVGqOaJERMsr3405uFL0k/ZqoG0DtVT\nL1kJ6kq1KNFxv802GKjz15poSF6eMDV1LQlttjv7bFFUjXaN4Tm3OkHyDAp2j62P\n/6dAHZf+wqpls8D14ytnq74P88NVQFltfsVialYH61K+dG0hu7HpAEy1sH5zh9Xm\n5qE3Y19OJPSojXXUomUVgLak4hKOipVt+iLIZIzXmEGRdfcT8mNj1udZ0DLor10s\nFhnhrWIVQaFJcqDtNlbwn5N9PiRt5bpOG51AO9D8Sinsr/w4DYefD4ion3H9GR+l\nX6mK7kZbciAUtDAk+B5jItRqa5+C3lxNfoNkvnl2YZ2l51HB9xziQetwKkLS7yCh\nptVJ3lymsBHUrc5ntS8RIvyrQt12n3CSY2ssZ7nkZ3dpQpxxHOPP/XDaZxjrCAuF\nJ9oBpzF5lokD8APdUxTYVcYjw8uxBY2xjJFleeRHXweUjih3VPsiIYrFGwZF5/Da\nKnWFEULtIBI1b6tWHjiS\n=rZh2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4f1beb9b414ca552aa6624b4394bcee886684a75\nparent 3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1783558708 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783558708 +0000\n\n[codex] Preserve reviewer when resuming threads (#30278)\n\n## Why\n\nA thread resumed without an explicit reviewer could pick up the reviewer\nfrom the current config instead of preserving the reviewer already in\nuse by the thread. After an app restart, this meant a thread running\nwith auto review could silently switch back to user review, and the next\nturn could continue under the wrong reviewer.\n\n## What changed\n\nPersist the effective reviewer with each turn and restore the latest\npersisted value when the thread resumes. If the resume request\nexplicitly provides a reviewer, that value still takes precedence.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Added a regression test that starts a thread with auto review, records\na turn, restarts with user review in config, resumes without an\noverride, and verifies that auto review is preserved.\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_preserves_persisted_approvals_reviewer`\n- Clippy for the affected crates","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:58:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0746e8a34574b4bf4721672c97fc6a94fd8bfad8/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737"}]},{"sha":"3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNmYTkwNjY1ZmViNTkzMTU1NzhmOWYyODJhMDljN2NlNTRkZGY3Mzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:17:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-09T00:17:38Z"},"message":"test: add delayed exec-server transport (#31427)\n\n## Why\n\nMacrobenchmarks benefit from having a way to exercise remote-executor\nlatency without depending on Docker.\n\nThis is a very minimal first cut, if we find that simulating network\nconditions is useful we can always expand this scope or switch to a more\nrobust network shaping approach.\n\n## What\n\n- add a package-local exec-server binary for Cargo and Bazel test\nfixtures\n- add a host-local WebSocket exec-server fixture and fixed-delay\ninterposer\n- let TestAppServer route its auto environment through that delayed\nWebSocket transport\n- cover the delayed thread/start path through the public app-server API\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#31425 test: add TestAppServer\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31425)\n2. [#31427 test: add delayed exec-server\ntransport](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31427)\n3. [#31295 bench: add cold skill load\nmacrobenchmark](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31295)\n4. [#31428 bench: add e2e benchmark\nentrypoints](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31428)\n5. [#31429 ci: smoke Bazel e2e\nbenchmarks](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31429)","tree":{"sha":"d20a5bfac7491666681218e507dee489e965ed56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d20a5bfac7491666681218e507dee489e965ed56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTuiiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASVYQAIotOGyIG1/zRokkd+ijv4h7\n2khfnxIBxzHBs9J4wV7S83ZqdVWJyrY7isBZ3GaHT7RkE+7be+PmCMhqdzpb4mW5\nlrdiOtmBnVPOQr3FihGhQofsM3wTTIqB78+w3oFwh96FXB7Bg3oWfim5qL8THq+/\nD+kfucLkWGjxOC3EmTyfEELXyMwvXt5rGDFjW8WwRkQBWCmXMGmdX4hv4G6bWeY1\nV78mDNrTKMkX1fwhwj1E3WdctEwaF0lfuGvELiRA/Z/n7mf6fwcGl0CSkx+wM3r3\n986B/cRshdelZ9OV8PUVjghLlIIMBP8LGMu0aILNNdFqixLSW9o43f+V7l31rEJ6\ngxvMWTVMyM12shk15Xpl0uVkY5TLuavsiHBSGlVuIH5yFH4GDJt9JwNx3boCiCuL\n8t1DKrEkVlJx1Z55JP9OCMkijUkTDev/uP3B4QeH28f/8RtGRnx0dAF0/F01NKPa\n7ly22UalaUYWlJuxC1Gb/g3sn65Lm31TIT6L6H/tMI8lGA+PRJaZcStuk7S6uTYz\nMfyO7LS1p9tEtlzOhmi+gva39sXnSe4Wd1zcyHQCtkFKSi1rXEsMa2hIePVg/vJi\nUWoVLo9a8KXQ2UUhEzyGwMLVSEmHDgm3yPGB3obRmaybd4sEXVYdjX4+7icceU67\nWpjNURd+P93GgB5dcO26\n=Mxa5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d20a5bfac7491666681218e507dee489e965ed56\nparent b7807380149d259f905dd23a7e188ba0148878b8\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1783556258 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783556258 +0000\n\ntest: add delayed exec-server transport (#31427)\n\n## Why\n\nMacrobenchmarks benefit from having a way to exercise remote-executor\nlatency without depending on Docker.\n\nThis is a very minimal first cut, if we find that simulating network\nconditions is useful we can always expand this scope or switch to a more\nrobust network shaping approach.\n\n## What\n\n- add a package-local exec-server binary for Cargo and Bazel test\nfixtures\n- add a host-local WebSocket exec-server fixture and fixed-delay\ninterposer\n- let TestAppServer route its auto environment through that delayed\nWebSocket transport\n- cover the delayed thread/start path through the public app-server API\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#31425 test: add TestAppServer\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31425)\n2. [#31427 test: add delayed exec-server\ntransport](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31427)\n3. [#31295 bench: add cold skill load\nmacrobenchmark](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31295)\n4. [#31428 bench: add e2e benchmark\nentrypoints](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31428)\n5. [#31429 ci: smoke Bazel e2e\nbenchmarks](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31429)","verified_at":"2026-07-09T00:17:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3fa90665feb59315578f9f282a09c7ce54ddf737/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","ava