url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77"}]},{"sha":"dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRiZDJkZjI3ZDEwODEwYjI3ZTE4MjhkMGIzZDRhYjg5NjQzZWFjNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:15:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:15:49Z"},"message":"test: migrate TestAppServer callers to builder (#31451)\n\n## Why\n\nKeep the TestAppServer builder API change reviewable by moving the\nrepository-wide caller migration into a mechanical follow-up.\n\n## What\n\n- replace TestAppServer constructor callsites with equivalent builder\nchains\n- preserve each caller's automatic-environment, args, program, env,\nmanaged-config, plugin-startup, and JSON-logging behavior\n- make no TestAppServer implementation changes\n\n## Validation\n\n- cargo check -p codex-app-server --tests\n\n## Cleanup stack\n\n1. [#31425 test: add TestAppServer\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31425)\n2. [#31451 test: migrate TestAppServer callers to\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31451)\n3. [#31452 test: remove TestAppServer\nconstructors](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31452)","tree":{"sha":"eb50642d02dc6573298a20fd8c3f03f21082bc0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eb50642d02dc6573298a20fd8c3f03f21082bc0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTZa1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA56kQAHLRNGNP14S3n2X8uyZK8wNd\nrgQWFpj8m2YEyBCxXLaKMMZZDm9mDX6loRSblE90fUmKnmLVdUVm7zaBL6We+HHW\ngMG7rRDDVFaH9n1pt1LrLxq8hl57KAAjVZJXP7I0xMiHPPKQ2J2qXXLM8Z7bnP1l\nMmdKGkqVZfKkcsbWa1j23U7SknDRGAnlvLkzQNqZUGMvI4u0cGK4i8hmV3MST9NW\nj+Bchahqlk1e959v+q24rBdFySvgmHwnbV+8UB3aDqMB/9jZwfJIYgmp30jKrQQA\nSsmLTx643kHdZTJqMHZXNXtGCP00z2q4rAVH5gIM9NuCG/tIcaAZ/61hJYgrR51p\n1qa69Ms1M/0Y2lHWIox9yXl//ky1GpDbI5VrzinC9tt2+Yyq9flVGdNvtSO9Nqvp\n575xdrFvD8hF1UzLJgaBbhXIlyAREy6jcmLHopCpoPLkN8g4TZtILNpfFuIDOOP0\nOnS2Q/8mXjFNlRV046phJfXwU9fSi6vPyT6O7nFDJzoj4mxOgpzNEMkK9zvGuUoT\nCN/qly/3hmOU92Gx2x019MsA8Wqm7wQMjrskJr5zfEcrB6quv9SuTFa5OtCK1f4M\nVQk/zjZArBohz2rhaEOgaK6TcA4GZEVWW0QGC1t33WvkPfRbt6P+J5YpLiRpaGji\nkDmJm0AzxfpB1inE6I2n\n=PhIK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb50642d02dc6573298a20fd8c3f03f21082bc0d\nparent e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1783469749 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783469749 +0000\n\ntest: migrate TestAppServer callers to builder (#31451)\n\n## Why\n\nKeep the TestAppServer builder API change reviewable by moving the\nrepository-wide caller migration into a mechanical follow-up.\n\n## What\n\n- replace TestAppServer constructor callsites with equivalent builder\nchains\n- preserve each caller's automatic-environment, args, program, env,\nmanaged-config, plugin-startup, and JSON-logging behavior\n- make no TestAppServer implementation changes\n\n## Validation\n\n- cargo check -p codex-app-server --tests\n\n## Cleanup stack\n\n1. [#31425 test: add TestAppServer\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31425)\n2. [#31451 test: migrate TestAppServer callers to\nbuilder](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31451)\n3. [#31452 test: remove TestAppServer\nconstructors](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31452)","verified_at":"2026-07-08T00:15:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dbd2df27d10810b27e1828d0b3d4ab89643eac77/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3"}]},{"sha":"e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2MGFmODFiNGZhODhjMTNjMGExZTRmNWUwMzFkY2I5ZTM0MzY0YzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:05:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:05:05Z"},"message":"refactor: unify external auth resolution (#31421)\n\n## Summary\n\nExternal auth had two paths: provider-command credentials were resolved\nthrough `ExternalAuth`, while app-provided ChatGPT credentials were\ninstalled separately and only used the provider for refresh.\n`ExternalAuth` also declared an auth mode independently from the\n`CodexAuth` value it returned, so the declaration and credentials could\ndisagree.\n\nThis change makes the provider-owned `CodexAuth` authoritative for\ninitial resolution, credential kind, and refresh.\n\n- remove `ExternalAuth::auth_mode` and require providers to return their\ncurrent auth from `resolve`\n- route external auth registration, resolution, and unauthorized refresh\nthrough `AuthManager::set_external_auth`\n- keep the last resolved credential with its provider so synchronous\nconsumers and unauthorized recovery observe the credential's actual mode\n- make the app-server bridge own both initial and refreshed ChatGPT\ncredentials, and detach it on logout\n- keep model listing free of auth-refresh side effects, including in\noffline mode\n\nProvider-command auth still follows its configured cache interval.\nApp-provided ChatGPT auth still asks the parent app once after a `401`\nand retries the request once.\n\nStacked on #31355.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-login`\n- `just test -p codex-models-manager`\n- focused `codex-app-server` tests for external login/logout,\nunauthorized refresh, and workspace mismatch","tree":{"sha":"fc2897d2bb43d150cceba36c343c1f9f6f73572f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fc2897d2bb43d150cceba36c343c1f9f6f73572f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTZQxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASxYQAC+8wUkPUwM3Tz3QPjqQcmif\n9i4ubsg5zwjrvEX8zIhenfungBzkoJac8/CxCwO7n8d5mgQMxQupk9av8TpLJWK8\nVjVumP4oZkOpNgnA1u364Lr33RUkwTQPLTG980HviOwNQRLpPRBBQLw4wLkBt5CN\nGVSuq+wGP0ZOJ035anqjswPkdXHujs7PXOvpAkpRsm0QNUhV2t8833tXqj/zMvTL\nnoq9H1jRoCSnk+VqSyEyQuJIFlYaNy45n8Rjvv6FqoLVQxxuaLdBnHsd7CYwP+s1\n2drcvY3ADir4aDwF4vqngeIeKbtxLk7YLi8v5eNePn6H9G3J+m54RJ3TTJ+2uisZ\na20cMjGuMONZXwoPmSHtrjPzZzDrlike9JyL6iL0OM9s0KQCEBIfZrBiHyI4onK9\nYqluPAjZWgKKju8tbLBM4hh06YGHraqGk0kvma46m8JNM/+TcTc/zPPzq45RTQEg\n3MHAE7iUtCCcuCMQoE2PkkxiugRfUmrTWrWw0yijFSBH1XRTur4ut/9YYKIGZ1ZU\nT+zO0FeArobEXY4E5r44Fd0RpA4oYXIX5NOGpN7n4AP5WyvST18Cu83wtNHXTbYT\nWxrlSjONa1iGYWHfCo5/GKJOPqliSfoRTXyQc4z5LN2xgcBe1SWtd1QtCJAt9+8S\nwWzh3ct12CDuilNGAMCq\n=UcZA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fc2897d2bb43d150cceba36c343c1f9f6f73572f\nparent 77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1783469105 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783469105 -0700\n\nrefactor: unify external auth resolution (#31421)\n\n## Summary\n\nExternal auth had two paths: provider-command credentials were resolved\nthrough `ExternalAuth`, while app-provided ChatGPT credentials were\ninstalled separately and only used the provider for refresh.\n`ExternalAuth` also declared an auth mode independently from the\n`CodexAuth` value it returned, so the declaration and credentials could\ndisagree.\n\nThis change makes the provider-owned `CodexAuth` authoritative for\ninitial resolution, credential kind, and refresh.\n\n- remove `ExternalAuth::auth_mode` and require providers to return their\ncurrent auth from `resolve`\n- route external auth registration, resolution, and unauthorized refresh\nthrough `AuthManager::set_external_auth`\n- keep the last resolved credential with its provider so synchronous\nconsumers and unauthorized recovery observe the credential's actual mode\n- make the app-server bridge own both initial and refreshed ChatGPT\ncredentials, and detach it on logout\n- keep model listing free of auth-refresh side effects, including in\noffline mode\n\nProvider-command auth still follows its configured cache interval.\nApp-provided ChatGPT auth still asks the parent app once after a `401`\nand retries the request once.\n\nStacked on #31355.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-login`\n- `just test -p codex-models-manager`\n- focused `codex-app-server` tests for external login/logout,\nunauthorized refresh, and workspace mismatch","verified_at":"2026-07-08T00:05:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e60af81b4fa88c13c0a1e4f5e031dcb9e34364c3/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86"}]},{"sha":"77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc3Yjc2NmM2ZWU2ZDFhN2NlOTA5MmQwNmVkYzA5ZTg1OTJlNTlhODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:02:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-07-08T00:02:16Z"},"message":"ci: parameterize Cargo target paths (#31332)\n\n## Why\n\nPrepare CI jobs for a later build-output relocation without changing\nwhere they write today.\n\n## What\n\n- Export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` from `setup-ci` at the existing\n`codex-rs/target` path.\n- Route nextest, release, artifact, and signing paths through\n`CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n- Require V8 staging callers to pass an explicit target directory while\npreserving the existing upstream path.\n\n## Manual validation\n\n- Ran `just test-github-scripts`.\n- Parsed GitHub Actions YAML with `yq`.\n\n## Stack\n\n- [#31332](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31332) — parameterize\nCargo target paths\n- [#31356](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31356) — Windows 2025\nrunner bump\n- [#31357](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31357) — Dev Drive I/O\nrouting","tree":{"sha":"494b3817067c1ca25e3a77846406979bef46fdf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/494b3817067c1ca25e3a77846406979bef46fdf1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTZOICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkfcQALEBdvr4Fhj/2ibFIId/ddoI\nwVWeRekjAmTPHk0OpbXexBv6ihcNOK1jMSRy/REgCsVU2dfTuTlittgG1HzTKdZW\nZCRkeLRmpkzwjdV1pPkUGcSSqXKRtU8xEOfJERPsstz3bPOfoBGElN9y1bUEjhqX\nASh4pXAh080L8KGaEre5/pTtW96ezQIRSqzVVvQDpUm6OqsgbkWom2alE4XDglQO\nS7x614MH1fMrHc2Jo+ledBWtMJPpqyqBxC4zPgEZWy9Wpj6+mqhEVt9Tm9yLyJrY\nzQs43ELr0/h58ioD9GNLXaug4rX94mic05Oo39h3HvenkZ5zhOu3x5ePB7iAFegb\nS7ywTne0tM3LpW/jNWtUisYnIFuclMxxb6OVhF0JWboXs+Qk/xcsE1UBl9N/XWv6\nz9+XqcJfQLuzueyjjN8Y/RPyiqTzH1WJU8WerhozPv//avZbZN8CO9fztY5QH4J8\nCdOTOnkhgGq+eLFNZStAUkEiwVxoF602y5XYmbr6MCTix3RnU1OBSNNGuW8QZ0sg\nBzV8nDNKujbjaU5rbkdOXKdXZVTOq4qhVekuiBzSzMgaQ60blUKJtq0MhIqW6/Hw\n0WRf0eh8rpnwfZAVa3yt+WfOMC72ptmil13e6o7K9JSHH/ErCjjH+Crqr0SlIGyf\n/kFKMFitRyxCCUDoWbda\n=yQY3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 494b3817067c1ca25e3a77846406979bef46fdf1\nparent 49f5cb0026599db7317e3778b33d8604a80c9f69\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1783468936 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783468936 +0000\n\nci: parameterize Cargo target paths (#31332)\n\n## Why\n\nPrepare CI jobs for a later build-output relocation without changing\nwhere they write today.\n\n## What\n\n- Export `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` from `setup-ci` at the existing\n`codex-rs/target` path.\n- Route nextest, release, artifact, and signing paths through\n`CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n- Require V8 staging callers to pass an explicit target directory while\npreserving the existing upstream path.\n\n## Manual validation\n\n- Ran `just test-github-scripts`.\n- Parsed GitHub Actions YAML with `yq`.\n\n## Stack\n\n- [#31332](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31332) — parameterize\nCargo target paths\n- [#31356](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31356) — Windows 2025\nrunner bump\n- [#31357](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/31357) — Dev Drive I/O\nrouting","verified_at":"2026-07-08T00:02:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77b766c6ee6d1a7ce9092d06edc09e8592e59a86/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://